<?xml version="1.0"?>
<body language="English">
	<row id="msg_0805_00000" index="0">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">garbage</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
		<language name="日本語"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00001" index="1">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For some time after its birth, it\ngrows by gaining nourishment from\nthe seed on its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00002" index="2">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the bud on its back starts\nswelling, a sweet aroma wafts to\nindicate the flower’s coming bloom.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00003" index="3">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">After a rainy day, the flower on\nits back smells stronger. The\nscent attracts other Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00004" index="4">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The fire on the tip of its tail is a\nmeasure of its life. If healthy,\nits tail burns intensely.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00005" index="5">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In the rocky mountains where\nCHARMELEON live, their fiery\ntails shine at night like stars.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00006" index="6">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that CHARIZARD’s fire\nburns hotter if it has\nexperienced harsh battles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00007" index="7">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shelters itself in its shell,\nthen strikes back with spouts of\nwater at every opportunity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00008" index="8">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to live 10,000 years.\nIts furry tail is popular as a\nsymbol of longevity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00009" index="9">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The jets of water it spouts from\nthe rocket cannons on its shell\ncan punch through thick steel.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00010" index="10">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It releases a stench from its red\nantenna to repel enemies. It\ngrows by molting repeatedly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00011" index="11">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A steel-hard shell protects its\ntender body. It quietly endures\nhardships while awaiting evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00012" index="12">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves the honey of flowers and\ncan locate flower patches that\nhave even tiny amounts of pollen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00013" index="13">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats its weight in leaves every\nday. It fends off attackers with\nthe needle on its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00014" index="14">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">While awaiting evolution, it\nhides from predators under\nleaves and in nooks of branches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00015" index="15">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its best attack involves flying\naround at high speed, striking with\npoison needles, then flying off.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00016" index="16">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is docile and prefers to avoid\nconflict. If disturbed, however,\nit can ferociously strike back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00017" index="17">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies over its wide territory in\nsearch of prey, downing it\nwith its highly developed claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00018" index="18">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By flapping its wings with all its\nmight, PIDGEOT can make a gust of\nwind capable of bending tall trees.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00019" index="19">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Cautious in the extreme, its\nhardy vitality lets it live in\nany kind of environment.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00020" index="20">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It whittles its constantly growing\nfangs by gnawing on hard things.\nIt can chew apart cinder walls.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00021" index="21">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flaps its small wings busily to\nfly. Using its beak, it searches\nin grass for prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00022" index="22">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the stamina to fly all\nday on its broad wings. It\nfights by using its sharp beak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00023" index="23">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sneaks through grass without\nmaking a sound and strikes\nunsuspecting prey from behind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00024" index="24">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The pattern on its belly is for\nintimidation. It constricts foes\nwhile they are frozen in fear.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00025" index="25">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in forests with others.\nIt stores electricity in the\npouches on its cheeks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00026" index="26">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It turns aggressive if it has too\nmuch electricity in its body. It\ndischarges power through its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00027" index="27">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To protect itself from attackers,\nit curls up into a ball. It lives in\narid regions with minimal rainfall.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00028" index="28">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It curls up, then rolls into foes\nwith its back. Its sharp spines\ninflict severe damage.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00029" index="29">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">While it does not prefer to fight,\neven one drop of the poison it\nsecretes from barbs can be fatal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00030" index="30">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it senses danger, it raises\nall the barbs on its body. These\nbarbs grow slower than NIDORINO’s.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00031" index="31">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its entire body is armored with\nhard scales. It will protect the\nyoung in its burrow with its life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00032" index="32">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It scans its surroundings by\nraising its ears out of the grass.\nIts toxic horn is for protection.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00033" index="33">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a violent disposition and\nstabs foes with its horn, which\noozes poison upon impact.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00034" index="34">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One swing of its mighty tail can\nsnap a telephone pole as if it were\na matchstick.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00035" index="35">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Thought to live with others on\nquiet mountains, it is popular\nfor its adorable nature.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00036" index="36">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Rarely seen by people, it is\nsaid to be drawn by the full\nmoon to play at deserted lakes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00037" index="37">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It controls balls of fire. As it\ngrows, its six tails split from\ntheir tips to make more tails.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00038" index="38">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its nine tails are said to be\nimbued with a mystic power.\nIt can live for a thousand years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00039" index="39">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it wavers its big, round\neyes, it begins singing a lullaby\nthat makes everyone drowsy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00040" index="40">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its fine fur feels sublime to the\ntouch. It can expand its body by\ninhaling air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00041" index="41">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Even though it has no eyes, it can\nsense obstacles using ultrasonic\nwaves it emits from its mouth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00042" index="42">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves the blood of humans and\nPokémon. It flies around at night\nin search of neck veins.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00043" index="43">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It often plants its root feet in the\nground during the day and sows\nseeds as it walks about at night.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00044" index="44">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The honey it drools from its mouth\nsmells so atrocious, it can curl\nnoses more than a mile away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00045" index="45">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its petals are the largest in the\nworld. As it walks, it scatters\nextremely allergenic pollen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00046" index="46">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Mushrooms named tochukaso grow\non its back. They grow along\nwith the host PARAS.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00047" index="47">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mushroom grown larger than the\nhost’s body controls PARASECT.\nIt scatters poisonous spores.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00048" index="48">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its big eyes are actually clusters\nof tiny eyes. At night, its kind is\ndrawn by light.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00049" index="49">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flutters its wings to scatter\ndustlike scales. The scales leach\ntoxins if they contact skin.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00050" index="50">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that lives underground.\nBecause of its dark habitat, it is\nrepelled by bright sunlight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00051" index="51">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its three heads move alternately,\ndriving it through tough soil to\ndepths of over 60 miles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00052" index="52">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is nocturnal in nature. If it\nspots something shiny, its eyes\nglitter brightly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00053" index="53">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very haughty Pokémon. Among\nfans, the size of the jewel in its\nforehead is a topic of much talk.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00054" index="54">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its usual headache worsens, it\nstarts exhibiting odd powers. It\ncan’t remember doing so, however.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00055" index="55">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that lives in lakes.\nIt swims faster than any human\nswimming champion.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00056" index="56">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in treetop colonies.\nIf one becomes enraged, the whole\ncolony rampages for no reason.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00057" index="57">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grows angry if you see its eyes\nand gets angrier if you run. If you\nbeat it, it gets even madder.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00058" index="58">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon with a loyal nature.\nIt will remain motionless until it is\ngiven an order by its Trainer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00059" index="59">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its proud and regal appearance\nhas captured the hearts of\npeople since long ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00060" index="60">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its skin is so thin, its internal\norgans are visible. It has trouble\nwalking on its newly grown feet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00061" index="61">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The spiral pattern on its belly\nsubtly undulates. Staring at it\ngradually causes drowsiness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00062" index="62">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With its extremely tough muscles,\nit can keep swimming in the Pacific\nOcean without resting.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00063" index="63">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sleeps for 18 hours a day.\nEven when awake, it teleports\nitself while remaining seated.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00064" index="64">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If one is nearby, an eerie shadow\nappears on TV screens. Seeing the\nshadow is said to bring bad luck.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00065" index="65">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its superb memory lets it recall\neverything it has experienced from\nbirth. Its IQ exceeds 5,000.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00066" index="66">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It hefts a GRAVELER repeatedly to\nstrengthen its entire body. It\nuses every type of martial arts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00067" index="67">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MACHOKE’s boundless power is very\ndangerous, so it wears a belt that\nsuppresses its energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00068" index="68">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It punches with its four arms at\nblinding speed. It can launch\n1,000 punches in two seconds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00069" index="69">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It prefers hot and humid\nenvironments. It is quick at\ncapturing prey with its vines.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00070" index="70">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that appears to be a\nplant. It captures unwary prey by\ndousing them with a toxic powder.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00071" index="71">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It pools in its mouth a fluid with\na honeylike scent, which is really\nan acid that dissolves anything.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00072" index="72">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is virtually composed of\nwater. It shoots strange beams\nfrom its crystal-like eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00073" index="73">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With 80 tentacles for ensnaring\nvictims, it prevents escape until\nthe prey is weakened by poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00074" index="74">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Many live on mountain trails\nand remain half buried while\nkeeping an eye on climbers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00075" index="75">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">GRAVELER make their homes on\nsheer cliff faces by gouging out\nnumerous horizontal holes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00076" index="76">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sheds its hide once a year.\nIts boulderlike body is so tough,\neven dynamite can’t harm it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00077" index="77">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">About an hour after birth, its\nfiery mane and tail grow out,\ngiving it an impressive appearance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00078" index="78">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gallops at nearly 150 mph.\nWith its mane blazing ferociously,\nit races as if it were an arrow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00079" index="79">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although slow, it is skilled at\nfishing with its tail. It does not\nfeel pain if its tail is bitten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00080" index="80">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Though usually dim witted, it\nseems to become inspired if the\nSHELLDER on its tail bites down.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00081" index="81">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The units at its sides generate\nelectromagnetic waves that keep it\nairborne. It feeds on electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00082" index="82">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is actually three MAGNEMITE\nlinked by magnetism. A group can\nset off a magnetic storm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00083" index="83">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can’t live without the stalk it\nholds. That’s why it defends the\nstalk from attackers with its life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00084" index="84">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The brains in its two heads appear\nto communicate emotions to each\nother with a telepathic power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00085" index="85">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When DODUO evolves into this odd\nbreed, one of its heads splits into\ntwo. It runs at nearly 40 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00086" index="86">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that lives on icebergs.\nIt swims in the sea using the point\non its head to break up ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00087" index="87">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In snow, the pure white coat\ncovering its body obscures it from\npredators.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00088" index="88">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was born when sludge in a dirty\nstream was exposed to the moon’s\nX-rays. It appears among filth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00089" index="89">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A toxic fluid seeps from its body.\nThe fluid instantly kills plants and\ntrees on contact.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00090" index="90">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swims backward by opening and\nclosing its two shells. Its large\ntongue is always kept hanging out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00091" index="91">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It fights by keeping its shell\ntightly shut for protection and\nby shooting spikes to repel foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00092" index="92">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon’s body is 95% made up\nof gases, which are blown away by\nstrong gusts of wind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00093" index="93">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can slip through any obstacle.\nIt lurks inside walls to keep an\neye on its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00094" index="94">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It hides in shadows. It is said\nthat if GENGAR is hiding, it cools\nthe area by nearly 10 degrees F.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00095" index="95">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it travels underground, it\ncauses rumbling and tremors.\nIt can move at 50 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00096" index="96">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can tell what people are\ndreaming by sniffing with its big\nnose. It loves fun dreams.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00097" index="97">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Seeing its swinging pendulum can\ninduce sleep in three seconds,\neven in someone who just woke up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00098" index="98">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in burrows dug on sandy\nbeaches. Its pincers fully grow\nback if they are broken in battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00099" index="99">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The larger pincer has 10,000-\nhorsepower strength. However, it\nis so heavy, it is difficult to aim.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00100" index="100">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It looks just like a Poké Ball.\nIt is dangerous because it may\nelectrocute or explode on touch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00101" index="101">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is known to drift on winds if it\nis bloated to bursting with stored\nelectricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00102" index="102">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its six eggs converse using\ntelepathy. They can quickly gather\nif they become separated.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00103" index="103">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is called “The Walking Jungle.”\nIf a head grows too big, it falls\noff and becomes an EXEGGCUTE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00104" index="104">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it thinks of its dead mother,\nit cries. Its crying makes the\nskull it wears rattle hollowly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00105" index="105">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">From its birth, this savage Pokémon\nconstantly holds bones. It is\nskilled in using them as weapons.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00106" index="106">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its legs can stretch double.\nFirst-time foes are startled by\nits extensible reach.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00107" index="107">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The arm-twisting punches it throws\npulverize even concrete. It rests\nafter three minutes of fighting.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00108" index="108">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Instead of hands, it uses its\ntongue, which is twice its height.\nIts sticky saliva grips anything.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00109" index="109">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Lighter-than-air gases in its body\nkeep it aloft. The gases not only\nsmell, they are also explosive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00110" index="110">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grows by feeding on gases\nreleased by garbage. Though very\nrare, triplets have been found.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00111" index="111">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is clad in a thick hide,\nand its tackles topple buildings.\nUnfortunately, it is not smart.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00112" index="112">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its brain developed after it stood\nup on its hind legs. Its drill horn\nbores tunnels through solid rock.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00113" index="113">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to deliver happiness.\nBeing compassionate, it shares its\neggs with injured people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00114" index="114">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is shrouded by blue vines.\nNo one has seen the face hidden\nbehind this growth of vines.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00115" index="115">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It raises its offspring in its belly\npouch. It lets the baby out to\nplay only when it feels safe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00116" index="116">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes its nest in the shade of\ncorals. If it senses danger, it\nspits murky ink and flees.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00117" index="117">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its spines provide protection.\nIts fins and bones are prized as\ntraditional medicine ingredients.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00118" index="118">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swims elegantly by flittering\nits tail fin as if it were a dress.\nIt has the look of a queen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00119" index="119">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes its nest by hollowing out\nboulders in streams with its horn.\nIt defends its eggs with its life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00120" index="120">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its body is torn, it can grow\nback if the red core remains.\nThe core flashes at midnight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00121" index="121">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">At the center of its body is a red\ncore, which sends mysterious\nradio signals into the night sky.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00122" index="122">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is a pantomime expert that can\ncreate invisible but solid walls\nusing miming gestures.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00123" index="123">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is nearly impossible to parry\nits attacking scythes. Its\nmovements are like a ninja’s.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00124" index="124">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its cries sound like human speech.\nHowever, it is impossible to tell\nwhat it is trying to say.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00125" index="125">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Half of all blackouts occur when\nthis Pokémon appears at power\nplants and eats electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00126" index="126">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Born in the spout of a volcano,\nits body is covered by flames\nthat shimmer like the sun.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00127" index="127">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grips prey with its pincers\nuntil the prey is torn in half.\nWhat it can’t tear, it tosses far.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00128" index="128">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once it takes aim at its foe, it\nmakes a headlong charge. It is\nfamous for its violent nature.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00129" index="129">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to be the world’s\nweakest Pokémon. No one knows why\nit has managed to survive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00130" index="130">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once it appears, its rage never\nsettles until it has razed the\nfields and mountains around it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00131" index="131">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves crossing the sea with\npeople and Pokémon on its back.\nIt understands human speech.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00132" index="132">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the ability to reconstitute\nits entire cellular structure to\ntransform into whatever it sees.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00133" index="133">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A rare Pokémon that adapts to\nharsh environments by taking on\ndifferent evolutionary forms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00134" index="134">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has evolved to be suitable for\nan aquatic life. It can invisibly\nmelt away into water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00135" index="135">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It controls 10,000-volt power\nand can raise all the fur on its\nbody as if it were sharp needles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00136" index="136">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a flame sac in its body.\nIts body temperature tops 1,650\ndegrees Fahrenheit before battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00137" index="137">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The world’s first artificially\ncreated Pokémon. It can travel\nthrough electronic space.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00138" index="138">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that was resurrected\nfrom a fossil using modern science.\nIt swam in ancient seas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00139" index="139">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is thought that this Pokémon\nbecame extinct because its spiral\nshell grew too large.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00140" index="140">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is thought to have inhabited\nbeaches 300 million years ago.\nIt is protected by a stiff shell.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00141" index="141">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is thought that this Pokémon\ncame onto land because its\nprey adapted to life on land.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00142" index="142">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that roamed the skies\nin the dinosaur era. Its teeth are\nlike saw blades.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00143" index="143">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its stomach can digest any kind\nof food, even if it happens to be\nmoldy or rotten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00144" index="144">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A legendary bird Pokémon.\nIt can create blizzards by\nfreezing moisture in the air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00145" index="145">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A legendary Pokémon that is said\nto live in thunderclouds. It freely\ncontrols lightning bolts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00146" index="146">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One of the legendary bird Pokémon.\nIt is said that its appearance\nindicates the coming of spring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00147" index="147">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is called the “Mirage Pokémon”\nbecause so few have seen it.\nIts shed skin has been found.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00148" index="148">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its body takes on an aura, the\nweather changes instantly. It is\nsaid to live in seas and lakes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00149" index="149">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to make its home\nsomewhere in the sea. It guides\ncrews of shipwrecks to shore.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00150" index="150">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon created by recombining\nMEW’s genes. It’s said to have the\nmost savage heart among Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00151" index="151">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it can use all kinds of\nmoves, many scientists believe MEW\nto be the ancestor of Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00152" index="152">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses the leaf on its head to\ndetermine the temperature and\nhumidity. It loves to sunbathe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00153" index="153">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The buds that ring its neck give\noff a spicy aroma that perks\npeople up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00154" index="154">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its breath has the fantastic\nability to revive dead plants and\nflowers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00155" index="155">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a timid nature. If it is\nstartled, the flames on its back\nburn more vigorously.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00156" index="156">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It intimidates foes with the heat\nof its flames. The fire burns more\nstrongly when it readies to fight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00157" index="157">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks using blasts of fire.\nIt creates heat shimmers with\nintense fire to hide itself.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00158" index="158">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the habit of biting anything\nwith its developed jaws. Even its\nTrainer needs to be careful.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00159" index="159">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once it bites down, it won’t let go\nuntil it loses its fangs. New fangs\nquickly grow into place.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00160" index="160">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It usually moves slowly, but it\ngoes at blinding speed when it\nattacks and bites prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00161" index="161">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a very nervous nature.\nIt stands up high on its tail so it\ncan scan wide areas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00162" index="162">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The mother puts its offspring to\nsleep by curling up around them.\nIt corners foes with speed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00163" index="163">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It always stands on one foot.\nEven when attacked, it does not\nbrace itself using both feet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00164" index="164">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its eyes are special. They can\npick out objects as long as there\nis the tiniest amount of light.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00165" index="165">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is so timid, it can’t move if it\nisn’t with a swarm of others. It\nconveys its feelings with scent.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00166" index="166">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses starlight as energy. When\nmore stars appear at night, the\npatterns on its back grow larger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00167" index="167">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sets a trap by spinning a web\nwith thin but strong silk. It waits\nmotionlessly for prey to arrive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00168" index="168">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attaches silk to its prey and\nsets it free. Later, it tracks the\nsilk to the prey and its friends.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00169" index="169">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Having four wings enables it to fly\nfaster and more quietly. It turns\nactive when the night comes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00170" index="170">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It discharges positive and\nnegative electricity from its\nantenna tips to shock its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00171" index="171">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">LANTURN’s light can shine up from\ngreat depths. It is nicknamed\n“The Deep-Sea Star.”</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00172" index="172">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The electric pouches on its cheeks\nare still small. They cannot store\nmuch electricity yet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00173" index="173">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its silhouette is like a star.\nIt is believed to arrive riding on\nshooting stars.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00174" index="174">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a soft and bouncy body.\nOnce it starts bouncing, it\nbecomes impossible to stop.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00175" index="175">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its shell is said to be stuffed\nwith happiness that it shares with\nkindhearted people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00176" index="176">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to appear in front of\nkindly people to scatter a glowing\ndown called “joy dust.”</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00177" index="177">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It picks food from cactus plants,\ndeftly avoiding buds and spines.\nIt seems to skip about to move.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00178" index="178">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This odd Pokémon can see both\nthe past and the future. It eyes\nthe sun’s movement all day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00179" index="179">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its fluffy coat swells to double\nwhen static electricity builds up.\nTouching it can be shocking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00180" index="180">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its coat becomes fully charged\nwith electricity, its tail lights up.\nIt fires hair that zaps on impact.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00181" index="181">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The tip of its tail shines brightly.\nIn the olden days, people sent\nsignals using the tail’s light.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00182" index="182">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the heavy rainfall season\nends, it is drawn out by warm\nsunlight to dance in the open.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00183" index="183">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using its tail as a float, it dives\nunderwater. It likes eating plants\nthat grow on river bottoms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00184" index="184">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in rivers and lakes. In\nwater, its coloring and patterns\ntrick the vision of foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00185" index="185">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Despite appearing to be a tree,\nits body is closer to rocks and\nstones. It is very weak to water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00186" index="186">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gathers groups of others as\ntheir leader. Its cries make\nPOLIWAG obey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00187" index="187">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It drifts on winds. It is said that\nwhen HOPPIP gather in fields and\nmountains, spring is on the way.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00188" index="188">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It blooms when the weather warms.\nIt floats in the sky to soak up as\nmuch sunlight as possible.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00189" index="189">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Blown by seasonal winds, it\ncircles the globe, scattering\ncotton spores as it goes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00190" index="190">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses its tail to pluck fruits\nthat are out of reach. Its tail is\nmore adept than its real hands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00191" index="191">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It suddenly falls out of the sky in\nthe morning. A year after a cold\nsummer, their population explodes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00192" index="192">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gets energy from warm sunlight\nand is known for its habit of\nmoving in pursuit of it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00193" index="193">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its eyes can see 360 degrees\nwithout moving its head. It won’t\nmiss prey--even those behind it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00194" index="194">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in cold water, half\nburying itself in mud at the\nbottom to sleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00195" index="195">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a sluggish nature. It lies\nat the river’s bottom, waiting for\nprey to stray into its mouth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00196" index="196">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its fur has the look and feel of\nvelvet. The orb on its forehead\nglows when it uses psycho-power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00197" index="197">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The light of the moon changed\nEEVEE’s genetic structure. It\nlurks in darkness for prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00198" index="198">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is believed that seeing this\nPokémon at night will bring\nabout ominous occurrences.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00199" index="199">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Being bitten by SHELLDER gave it\nintelligence comparable to that of\naward-winning scientists.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00200" index="200">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves to sneak up on people\nlate at night, then startle them\nwith its shrieklike cry.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00201" index="201">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Shaped like ancient writing, it is\na huge mystery whether\nlanguage or UNOWN came first.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00202" index="202">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It desperately tries to keep its\nblack tail hidden. It is said to be\nproof the tail hides a secret.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00203" index="203">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its tail also has a small brain.\nIt bites to repel any foe trying\nto sneak up on it from behind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00204" index="204">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It looks just like a pinecone.\nIts shell protects it from bird\nPokémon that peck it by mistake.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00205" index="205">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is encased in a steel shell. Its\npeering eyes are all that can be\nseen of its mysterious innards.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00206" index="206">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It digs into the ground with its\ntail and makes a mazelike nest.\nIt can fly just a little.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00207" index="207">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sails on the winds with its\nlimbs extended to strike from the\nsky. It aims for the prey’s face.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00208" index="208">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Tempered underground under\nhigh pressure and heat, its\nbody is harder than any metal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00209" index="209">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Small Pokémon flee from its scary\nface. It is, however, considered\nby women to be cute.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00210" index="210">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is timid in spite of its looks.\nIf it becomes enraged, however,\nit will strike with its huge fangs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00211" index="211">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shoots the poison spines on its\nbody in all directions. Its round\nform makes it a poor swimmer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00212" index="212">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a steel-hard body. It\nintimidates foes by upraising its\neye-patterned pincers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00213" index="213">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores berries in its shell.\nThe berries eventually ferment to\nbecome delicious juices.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00214" index="214">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gathers in forests to search\nfor tree sap, its favorite food.\nIt’s strong enough to hurl foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00215" index="215">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It feeds on eggs stolen from\nnests. Its sharply hooked claws\nrip vulnerable spots on prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00216" index="216">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lets honey soak into its paws\nso it can lick them all the time.\nEvery set of paws tastes unique.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00217" index="217">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In its territory, it leaves\nscratches on trees that bear\ndelicious berries or fruits.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00218" index="218">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is made of magma.\nIf it doesn’t keep moving, its\nbody will cool and harden.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00219" index="219">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body temperature is roughly\n18,000 degrees F. Flames spout\nfrom gaps in its hardened shell.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00220" index="220">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves eating mushrooms that\ngrow under dead grass. It also\nfinds hot springs while foraging.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00221" index="221">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its shaggy coat makes it unable\nto see. It checks surroundings\nwith its sensitive nose instead.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00222" index="222">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Many live in the clean seas of the\nsouth. They apparently can’t live\nin polluted waters.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00223" index="223">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It squirts water forcefully from\nits mouth to shoot down flying\nprey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00224" index="224">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in the gaps of boulders\nand in holes on the seafloor. Its\nsuction cups grip prey tightly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00225" index="225">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It carries food rolled up in its\ntail. It has the habit of sharing\nfood with people lost in mountains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00226" index="226">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the waves are calm, one may\nencounter a swarm of MANTINE\nswimming as if they are in flight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00227" index="227">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Despite being clad entirely in\niron-hard armor, it flies at\nspeeds over 180 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00228" index="228">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It conveys its feelings using\ndifferent cries. It works in a pack\nto cleverly take down prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00229" index="229">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Long ago, people imagined\nits eerie howls to be the call\nof the grim reaper.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00230" index="230">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in caves on the seafloor\nand creates giant whirlpools\nevery time it moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00231" index="231">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is strong despite its compact\nsize. It can easily pick up and\ncarry an adult human on its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00232" index="232">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks by curling up, then\nrolling into its foe. It can blow\napart a house in one hit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00233" index="233">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With planetary development\nsoftware installed, it became\ncapable of working in space.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00234" index="234">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Staring at its antlers creates\nan odd sensation as if one were\nbeing drawn into their centers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00235" index="235">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It marks its territory by using its\ntail like a paintbrush. There are\nmore than 5,000 different marks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00236" index="236">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is famous for its eagerness to\nfight and always nurses injuries\nfrom challenging larger foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00237" index="237">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It fights while spinning like a top.\nThe centrifugal force boosts its\ndestructive power by ten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00238" index="238">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It tests everything by touching\nwith its lips, which remember\nwhat it likes and dislikes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00239" index="239">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It generates electricity by\nwhirling its arms. However, it\ncan’t store the energy it makes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00240" index="240">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body temperature is around\n1,100 degrees F. It is healthy if\nit is breathing yellow flames.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00241" index="241">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that kids who drink\nMILTANK’s milk grow up to become\nhearty, healthy adults.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00242" index="242">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This kindhearted Pokémon\nnurses sick Pokémon to health.\nIt senses feelings of sadness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00243" index="243">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to have fallen with\nlightning. It can fire thunderbolts\nfrom the rain clouds on its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00244" index="244">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that when it roars, a\nvolcano erupts somewhere around\nthe globe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00245" index="245">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It races around the world to\npurify fouled water. It dashes\naway with the north wind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00246" index="246">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that eats soil. Once it\nhas eaten a large mountain, it\ngoes to sleep so it can grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00247" index="247">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is as hard as bedrock.\nBy venting pressurized gas, it can\nlaunch itself like a rocket.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00248" index="248">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it rampages, it knocks down\nmountains and buries rivers. Maps\nmust be redrawn afterward.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00249" index="249">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sleeps in a deep-sea trench.\nIf it flaps its wings, it is said to\ncause a 40-day storm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00250" index="250">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its feathers are in seven colors.\nIt is said that anyone seeing it is\npromised eternal happiness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00251" index="251">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the power to travel across\ntime, but it is said to appear only\nin peaceful times.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00252" index="252">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The soles of its feet are covered\nby countless tiny spikes, enabling\nit to walk on walls and ceilings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00253" index="253">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in dense jungles. While \nclosing in on its prey, it leaps\nfrom branch to branch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00254" index="254">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The leaves that grow on its arms\ncan slice down thick trees. It is\nwithout peer in jungle combat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00255" index="255">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A fire burns inside, so it feels\nvery warm to hug. It launches\nfireballs of 1,800 degrees F.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00256" index="256">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its kicking mastery lets it loose\n10 kicks per second. It emits\nsharp cries to intimidate foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00257" index="257">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Flames spout from its wrists,\nenveloping its knuckles. Its\npunches scorch its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00258" index="258">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To alert it, the fin on its head\nsenses the flow of water. It has\nthe strength to heft boulders.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00259" index="259">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its sturdy legs give it sure\nfooting, even in mud. It\nburrows into dirt to sleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00260" index="260">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can swim while towing a large\nship. It bashes down foes with a\nswing of its thick arms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00261" index="261">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon with a persistent\nnature, it chases its chosen prey\nuntil the prey becomes exhausted.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00262" index="262">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It chases down prey in a pack.\nIt will never disobey the commands\nof a skilled Trainer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00263" index="263">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It walks in zigzag fashion. It is\ngood at finding items in the\ngrass and even in the ground.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00264" index="264">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It charges prey at speeds over\n60 mph. However, because it can\nonly run straight, it often fails.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00265" index="265">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves to eat leaves. If it is\nattacked by a STARLY, it will defend\nitself with its spiked rear.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00266" index="266">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It anchors itself by wrapping\ntwigs with the silk from its body.\nIt motionlessly awaits evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00267" index="267">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has an aggressive nature. It\nstabs prey with its long, narrow\nmouth to drain the prey’s fluids.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00268" index="268">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is hot inside its cocoon. All\nthe cells in its body create the\nenergy for it to evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00269" index="269">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A nocturnal Pokémon. Drawn by\nstreetlights, they messily eat the\nleaves of trees lining boulevards.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00270" index="270">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It looks like an aquatic plant and\nserves as a ferry to Pokémon\nthat can’t swim.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00271" index="271">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a mischievous spirit. If it\nspots an angler, it will tug on the\nfishing line to interfere.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00272" index="272">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it hears festive music, all its\nmuscles fill with energy. It can’t\nhelp breaking out into a dance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00273" index="273">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it dangles from a tree\nbranch, it looks just like an acorn.\nIt enjoys scaring other Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00274" index="274">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The sound of its grass flute makes\nits listeners uneasy. It lives deep\nin forests.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00275" index="275">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By flapping its leafy fan, it can\nwhip up gusts of 100 ft/second\nthat can level houses.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00276" index="276">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a gutsy spirit that makes\nit bravely take on tough foes. It\nflies in search of warm climates.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00277" index="277">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It circles the sky in search of\nprey. When it spots one, it dives\nsteeply to catch the prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00278" index="278">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes its nest on steep sea\ncliffs. Riding updrafts, it soars\nto great heights.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00279" index="279">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It dips its large bill in the sea,\nthen scoops up numerous prey\nalong with water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00280" index="280">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses the horns on its head to\nsense human emotions. It is said to\nappear in front of cheerful people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00281" index="281">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is highly perceptive of its\nTrainer’s feelings. It dances when\nit is feeling happy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00282" index="282">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It will try to guard its trusted\nTrainer with its life. It has the\nability to see the future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00283" index="283">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It appears as if it is skating on\nwater. It draws prey with a sweet\nscent from the tip of its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00284" index="284">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its antennae have eye patterns\non them. Its four wings enable it\nto hover and fly in any direction.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00285" index="285">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It spouts poison spores from the\ntop of its head. These spores\ncause pain all over if inhaled.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00286" index="286">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its short arms stretch when it\nthrows punches. Its technique is\nequal to that of pro boxers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00287" index="287">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It spends nearly all its time in a\nday sprawled out. Just seeing it\nmakes one drowsy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00288" index="288">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its heart beats at a tenfold\ntempo, so it cannot sit still for\neven a moment.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00289" index="289">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The world’s laziest Pokémon. When\nit is lounging, it is actually saving\nenergy for striking back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00290" index="290">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grows underground, sensing\nits surroundings using antennae\ninstead of its virtually blind eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00291" index="291">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it moves so quickly, it\nsometimes becomes unseeable. It\ncongregates around tree sap.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00292" index="292">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A discarded bug shell that came to\nlife. Peering into the crack on its\nback is said to steal one’s spirit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00293" index="293">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Usually, its cries are like quiet\nmurmurs. If frightened, it shrieks\nat the same volume as a jet plane.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00294" index="294">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The shock waves from its cries can\ntip over trucks. It stamps its\nfeet to power up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00295" index="295">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its howls can be heard over six\nmiles away. It emits all sorts of\nnoises from the ports on its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00296" index="296">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It toughens its body by slamming\ninto thick trees. Many snapped\ntrees can be found near its nest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00297" index="297">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves to match power with\nbig-bodied Pokémon. It can knock a\ntruck flying with its arm thrusts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00298" index="298">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that lives by water.\nIt moves quickly on land by\nbouncing on its big tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00299" index="299">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its nose is a magnet. As a result,\nthis Pokémon always keeps its face\npointing north.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00300" index="300">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can’t stop itself from chasing\nmoving things, and it runs in a\ncircle, chasing its own tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00301" index="301">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is highly popular among female\nTrainers for its sublime fur.\nIt does not keep a nest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00302" index="302">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It hides in the darkness of caves.\nIts diet of gems has transformed\nits eyes into gemstones.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00303" index="303">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Attached to its head is a huge\nset of jaws formed by horns.\nIt can chew through iron beams.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00304" index="304">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It usually lives deep in mountains.\nHowever, hunger may drive it to\neat railroad tracks and cars.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00305" index="305">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For food, it digs up iron ore. It\nsmashes its steely body against\nothers to fight over territory.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00306" index="306">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">While seeking iron for food, it\ndigs tunnels by breaking through\nbedrock with its steel horns.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00307" index="307">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats just one berry a day.\nBy enduring hunger, its spirit is\ntempered and made sharper.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00308" index="308">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Through yoga training, it has\nhoned its sixth sense. Its\nmovements are elegant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00309" index="309">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using electricity stored in its fur,\nit stimulates its muscles to\nheighten its reaction speed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00310" index="310">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It discharges electricity from its\nmane. It creates a thundercloud\noverhead to drop lightning bolts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00311" index="311">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It cheers on friends with pom-poms\nmade of sparks. It drains power\nfrom telephone poles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00312" index="312">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It cheers on friends. If its\nfriends are losing, its body lets\noff more and more sparks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00313" index="313">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It communicates with others by\nlighting up its rear at night. It\nloves ILLUMISE’s sweet aroma.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00314" index="314">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With its sweet aroma, it guides\nVOLBEAT to draw signs with light in\nthe night sky.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00315" index="315">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">ROSELIA raised on clean drinking\nwater are known to grow vividly\ncolored flowers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00316" index="316">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Almost all its body is its stomach.\nIts harsh digestive juices quickly\ndissolve anything it swallows.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00317" index="317">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swallows anything whole.\nIt sweats toxic fluids from its\nfollicles to douse foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00318" index="318">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They swarm any foe that invades\ntheir territory. Their sharp fangs\ncan tear out boat hulls.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00319" index="319">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its fangs rip through sheet iron.\nIt swims at 75 mph and is known as\n“The Bully of the Sea.”</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00320" index="320">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">On sunny days, it lands on beaches\nto bounce like a ball and play.\nIt spouts water from its nose.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00321" index="321">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The biggest of all Pokémon.\nIt can dive to a depth of almost\n10,000 feet on only one breath.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00322" index="322">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its humped back stores intensely\nhot magma. In rain, the magma\ncools, slowing its movement.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00323" index="323">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has volcanoes on its back. If\nmagma builds up in its body, it\nshudders, then erupts violently.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00324" index="324">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It burns coal inside its shell for\nenergy. It blows out black soot if\nit is endangered.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00325" index="325">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bounces constantly, using its\ntail like a spring. The shock of\nbouncing keeps its heart beating.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00326" index="326">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses black pearls to amplify its\npsycho-power. It does an odd\ndance to gain control over foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00327" index="327">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">No two SPINDA have the same\npattern of spots. Its tottering\nstep fouls the aim of foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00328" index="328">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes a conical pit in desert\nsand and lies in wait at the bottom\nfor prey to come tumbling down.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00329" index="329">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It violently shudders its wings,\ngenerating ultrasonic waves to\ninduce headaches in people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00330" index="330">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It whips up sandstorms with\npowerful flaps of its wings. It is\nknown as “The Desert Spirit.”</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00331" index="331">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By storing water in its body, this\ndesert dweller can survive for 30\ndays without water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00332" index="332">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It becomes active at night,\nseeking prey that is exhausted\nfrom the day’s desert heat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00333" index="333">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its wings are like cotton tufts.\nIf it perches on someone’s head,\nit looks like a cotton hat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00334" index="334">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It looks like a fluffy cloud when\nit is in flight. It hums with its\nsoprano voice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00335" index="335">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has feuded with SEVIPER for\nmany generations. Its sharp claws\nare its biggest weapons.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00336" index="336">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For many generations, it has\nfeuded with ZANGOOSE. It whets its\nbladed tail on rocks for battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00337" index="337">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it turns active on nights\nof the full moon, it is said to have\nsome link to the lunar phases.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00338" index="338">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A new Pokémon species, rumored\nto be from the sun. It gives off\nlight while spinning.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00339" index="339">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It coats its entire body with a\nslimy fluid so it can squirm and\nslip away if grabbed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00340" index="340">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is very territorial. It repels\nfoes by setting off tremors that\nextend over a three-mile radius.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00341" index="341">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its hardy vitality enables it to\nadapt to any environment. Its\npincers will never release prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00342" index="342">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is a ruffian that uses its\npincers to pick up and toss out\nother Pokémon from its pond.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00343" index="343">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It moves by spinning on its foot.\nIt is a rare Pokémon that was\ndiscovered in ancient ruins.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00344" index="344">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ancient clay figurine that came\nto life as a Pokémon from exposure\nto a mysterious ray of light.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00345" index="345">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lived on the seafloor 100\nmillion years ago and was\nreanimated scientifically.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00346" index="346">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in the shallows of warm\nseas. When the tide goes out, it\ndigs up prey from beaches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00347" index="347">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon ancestor that was\nreanimated from a fossil. It lived\nin the sea and hunted with claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00348" index="348">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It went ashore after evolving.\nIts entire body is clad in a sturdy\narmor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00349" index="349">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is famous for its shabby\nappearance. While populous, they\ntend to cluster in set locations.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00350" index="350">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When people bicker, it is said to\narise from the depths of lakes to\nbecalm violent hearts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00351" index="351">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its appearance changes with the\nweather. Recently, its molecules\nwere found to be just like water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00352" index="352">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can freely change its body’s\ncolor. The zigzag pattern on its\nbelly doesn’t change, however.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00353" index="353">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves vengeful emotions and\nhangs in rows under the eaves of\nhouses where vengeful people live.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00354" index="354">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A doll that became a Pokémon over\nits grudge from being junked. It\nseeks the child that disowned it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00355" index="355">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It doggedly pursues its prey\nwherever it goes. However, the\nchase is abandoned at sunrise.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00356" index="356">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is hollow. It is said that\nthose who look into its body are\nsucked into the void.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00357" index="357">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it continually ate only\nits favorite fruit, the fruit\nstarted growing around its neck.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00358" index="358">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To knock foes flying, it makes the\nair shudder with its cries. It\nconverses using seven cries.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00359" index="359">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It senses coming disasters and\nappears before people only to\nwarn them of impending danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00360" index="360">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grows strong by pushing up\nagainst others en masse.\nIt loves eating sweet fruit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00361" index="361">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In the snow country, certain\nfolklore says a house will\nprosper if a SNORUNT lives there.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00362" index="362">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To protect itself, it clads its\nbody in an armor of ice, made\nby freezing moisture in the air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00363" index="363">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It rolls across ice floes to reach\nshore because its body is poorly\nshaped for swimming.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00364" index="364">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It habitually spins things on its\nnose. By doing so, it learns\ntextures and odors.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00365" index="365">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shatters ice with its big tusks.\nIts thick blubber repels not only\nthe cold, but also enemy attacks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00366" index="366">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes a single pearl during\nits lifetime. The pearl is said\nto amplify psychic power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00367" index="367">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives deep in the sea. With a\ntail shaped like a small fish, it\nattracts unsuspecting prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00368" index="368">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives at the bottom of the sea.\nIn the springtime, its pink body\nturns more vivid for some reason.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00369" index="369">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A rare Pokémon discovered during\na deep-sea exploration. It has not\nchanged in over 100 million years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00370" index="370">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in warm seas. It is said\nthat a couple finding this Pokémon\nwill be blessed with eternal love.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00371" index="371">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Dreaming of one day flying, it\npractices by leaping off cliffs\nevery day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00372" index="372">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Within its rugged shell, its cells\nhave begun changing. The shell\npeels off the instant it evolves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00373" index="373">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As a result of its long-held dream\nof flying, its cellular structure\nchanged, and wings grew out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00374" index="374">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It converses with others by using\nmagnetic pulses. In a swarm, they\nmove in perfect unison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00375" index="375">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is formed by two BELDUM joining\ntogether. Its steel body won’t be\nscratched if it collides with a jet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00376" index="376">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">METANG combined to form it.\nWith four brains, it has the\nintelligence of a supercomputer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00377" index="377">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its entire body is made of rock.\nIf any part chips off in battle, it\nattaches rocks to repair itself.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00378" index="378">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is made of ice from the\nice age. It controls frigid air of\n-328 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00379" index="379">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Tempered by pressure underground\nover tens of thousands of years,\nits body cannot be scratched.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00380" index="380">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is covered with a down\nthat can refract light in such a\nway that it becomes invisible.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00381" index="381">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A highly intelligent Pokémon.\nBy folding back its wings in flight,\nit can overtake jet planes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00382" index="382">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to have widened the\nseas by causing downpours. It had\nbeen asleep in a marine trench.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00383" index="383">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It had been asleep in underground\nmagma ever since it fiercely\nfought KYOGRE long ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00384" index="384">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in the ozone layer far\nabove the clouds and cannot be\nseen from the ground.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00385" index="385">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to have the ability to\ngrant any wish for just one week\nevery thousand years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00386" index="386">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An alien virus that fell to earth\non a meteor underwent a DNA\nmutation to become this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00387" index="387">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Made from soil, the shell on its\nback hardens when it drinks water.\nIt lives along lakes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00388" index="388">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives along water in forests. In\nthe daytime, it leaves the forest\nto sunbathe its treed shell.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00389" index="389">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Small Pokémon occasionally gather\non its unmoving back to begin\nbuilding their nests.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00390" index="390">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It agilely scales sheer cliffs to\nlive atop craggy mountains. Its\nfire is put out when it sleeps.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00391" index="391">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To intimidate attackers, it\nstretches the fire on its tail\nto make itself appear bigger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00392" index="392">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses a special kind of martial\narts involving all its limbs.\nIts fire never goes out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00393" index="393">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it is very proud, it hates\naccepting food from people. Its\nthick down guards it from cold.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00394" index="394">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives alone, away from others.\nApparently, every one of them\nbelieves it is the most important.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00395" index="395">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The three horns that extend from\nits beak attest to its power. The\nleader has the biggest horns.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00396" index="396">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They flock in great numbers.\nThough small, they flap their\nwings with great power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00397" index="397">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies around forests and fields\nin search of bug Pokémon.\nIt stays within a huge flock.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00398" index="398">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a savage nature. It will\ncourageously challenge foes that\nare much larger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00399" index="399">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With nerves of steel, nothing can\nperturb it. It is more agile and\nactive than it appears.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00400" index="400">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes its nest by damming\nstreams with bark and mud. It is\nknown as an industrious worker.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00401" index="401">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shakes its head back to front,\ncausing its antennae to hit each\nother and sound like a xylophone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00402" index="402">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crosses its knifelike arms in\nfront of its chest when it cries.\nIt can compose melodies ad lib.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00403" index="403">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">All of its fur dazzles if danger is\nsensed. It flees while the foe is\nmomentarily blinded.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00404" index="404">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its claws loose electricity with\nenough amperage to cause fainting.\nThey live in small groups.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00405" index="405">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has eyes that can see through\nanything. It spots and captures\nprey hiding behind objects.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00406" index="406">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Over the winter, it closes its bud\nand endures the cold. In spring,\nthe bud opens and releases pollen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00407" index="407">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attracts prey with a sweet\naroma, then downs it with\nthorny whips hidden in its arms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00408" index="408">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lived in jungles around 100\nmillion years ago. Its skull is as\nhard as iron.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00409" index="409">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its powerful head butt has enough\npower to shatter even the most\ndurable things upon impact.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00410" index="410">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that lived in jungles\naround 100 million years ago. Its\nfacial hide is extremely hard.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00411" index="411">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Any frontal attack is repulsed.\nIt is a docile Pokémon that\nfeeds on grass and berries.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00412" index="412">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To shelter itself from cold, wintry\nwinds, it covers itself with a cloak\nmade of twigs and leaves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00413" index="413">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When BURMY evolved, its cloak\nbecame a part of this Pokémon’s\nbody. The cloak is never shed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00414" index="414">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves the honey of flowers\nand steals honey collected by\nCOMBEE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00415" index="415">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon formed by three others.\nIt busily carries sweet floral\nhoney to VESPIQUEN.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00416" index="416">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its abdomen is a honeycomb for\ngrubs. It raises its grubs on\nhoney collected by COMBEE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00417" index="417">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes fur balls that crackle\nwith static electricity. It stores\nthem with berries in tree holes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00418" index="418">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a flotation sac that is\nlike an inflatable collar. It floats\non water with its head out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00419" index="419">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It floats using its well-developed\nflotation sac. It assists in the\nrescues of drowning people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00420" index="420">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The small ball holds the nutrients\nneeded for evolution. Apparently,\nit is very sweet and tasty.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00421" index="421">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It blooms during times of strong\nsunlight. It tries to make up for\neverything it endured as a bud.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00422" index="422">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its colors and shapes differ from\nregion to region. In the Sinnoh\nregion, two types are confirmed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00423" index="423">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a pliable body without any\nbones. If any part of its body is\ntorn off, it grows right back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00424" index="424">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To eat, it deftly shucks nuts\nwith its two tails. It rarely uses\nits arms now.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00425" index="425">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon formed by the spirits\nof people and Pokémon. It loves\ndamp, humid seasons.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00426" index="426">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s drowzy in daytime, but flies\noff in the evening in big groups.\nNo one knows where they go.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00427" index="427">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It slams foes by sharply uncoiling\nits rolled ears. It stings enough\nto make a grown-up cry in pain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00428" index="428">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An extremely cautious Pokémon.\nIt cloaks its body with its fluffy\near fur when it senses danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00429" index="429">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its cries sound like incantations.\nThose hearing it are tormented\nby headaches and hallucinations.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00430" index="430">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Becoming active at night, it is\nknown to swarm with numerous\nMURKROW in tow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00431" index="431">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It claws if displeased and purrs\nwhen affectionate. Its fickleness\nis very popular among some.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00432" index="432">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is a brazen brute that barges\nits way into another Pokémon’s\nnest and claims it as its own.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00433" index="433">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It emits cries by agitating an orb\nat the back of its throat.\nIt moves with flouncing hops.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00434" index="434">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It protects itself by spraying a\nnoxious fluid from its rear. The\nstench lingers for 24 hours.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00435" index="435">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sprays a vile-smelling fluid\nfrom the tip of its tail to attack.\nIts range is over 160 feet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00436" index="436">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Implements shaped like it were\ndiscovered in ancient tombs. It is\nunknown if they are related.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00437" index="437">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One caused a news sensation when\nit was dug up at a construction\nsite after a 2,000-year sleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00438" index="438">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It looks as if it is always crying.\nIt is actually adjusting its body’s\nfluid levels by eliminating excess.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00439" index="439">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It habitually mimics foes. Once\nmimicked, the foe cannot take its\neyes off this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00440" index="440">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves round white things.\nIt carries an egg-shaped rock in\nimitation of CHANSEY.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00441" index="441">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can learn and speak human\nwords. If they gather, they all\nlearn the same saying.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00442" index="442">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that was formed by 108\nspirits. It is bound to a fissure\nin an odd keystone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00443" index="443">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It nests in small, horizontal holes\nin cave walls. It pounces to catch\nprey that stray too close.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00444" index="444">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">There is a long-held belief that\nmedicine made from its scales will\nheal even incurable illnesses.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00445" index="445">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it folds up its body and\nextends its wings, it looks like a\njet plane. It flies at sonic speed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00446" index="446">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wolfs down its weight in food\nonce a day, swallowing food whole\nwith almost no chewing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00447" index="447">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The aura that emanates from its\nbody intensifies to alert others\nif it is afraid or sad.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00448" index="448">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the ability to sense the\nauras of all things.\nIt understands human speech.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00449" index="449">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in arid places. Instead\nof perspiration, it expels grainy\nsand from its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00450" index="450">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It blasts internally stored sand\nfrom ports on its body to create\na towering twister for attack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00451" index="451">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grips prey with its tail claws\nand injects poison. It tenaciously\nhangs on until the poison takes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00452" index="452">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the power in its clawed\narms to make scrap of a car. The\ntips of its claws release poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00453" index="453">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its cheeks hold poison sacs.\nIt tries to catch foes off guard\nto jab them with toxic fingers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00454" index="454">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its knuckle claws secrete a toxin\nso vile that even a scratch could\nprove fatal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00455" index="455">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attracts prey with its sweet-\nsmelling saliva, then chomps down.\nIt takes a whole day to eat prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00456" index="456">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">After long exposure to sunlight,\nthe patterns on its tail fins shine\nvividly when darkness arrives.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00457" index="457">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives on the deep-sea floor.\nIt attracts prey by flashing the\npatterns on its four tail fins.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00458" index="458">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A friendly Pokémon that captures\nthe subtle flows of seawater using\nits two antennae.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00459" index="459">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives on snowy mountains.\nHaving had little contact with\nhumans, it is boldly inquisitive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00460" index="460">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It whips up blizzards in mountains\nthat are always buried in snow.\nIt is the abominable snowman.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00461" index="461">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live in cold regions, forming\ngroups of four or five that hunt\nprey with impressive coordination.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00462" index="462">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It evolved from exposure to a\nspecial magnetic field.\nThree units generate magnetism.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00463" index="463">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wraps things with its extensible\ntongue. Getting too close to it\nwill leave you soaked with drool.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00464" index="464">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It puts rocks in holes in its palms\nand uses its muscles to shoot them.\nGEODUDE are shot at rare times.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00465" index="465">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It ensnares prey by extending\narms made of vines. Losing arms to\npredators does not trouble it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00466" index="466">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It pushes the tips of its two tails\nagainst the foe, then lets loose\nwith over 20,000 volts of power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00467" index="467">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It blasts fireballs of over 3,600\ndegrees F from the ends of its\narms. It lives in volcanic craters.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00468" index="468">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It will never appear where there\nis strife. Its sightings have\nbecome rare recently.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00469" index="469">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By churning its wings, it creates\nshock waves that inflict critical\ninternal injuries to foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00470" index="470">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Just like a plant, it uses\nphotosynthesis. As a result, it is\nalways enveloped in clear air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00471" index="471">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As a protective technique, it can\ncompletely freeze its fur to make\nits hairs stand like needles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00472" index="472">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It observes prey while hanging\ninverted from branches. When the\nchance presents itself, it swoops!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00473" index="473">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its impressive tusks are made of\nice. The population thinned when it\nturned warm after the ice age.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00474" index="474">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Additional software was installed\nto make it a better Pokémon.\nIt began acting oddly, however.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00475" index="475">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A master of courtesy and\nswordsmanship, it fights using\nextending swords on its elbows.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00476" index="476">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It exudes strong magnetism from\nall over. It controls three small\nunits called Mini-Noses.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00477" index="477">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The antenna on its head captures\nradio waves from the world of spirits\nthat command it to take people there.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00478" index="478">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It freezes foes with an icy breath\nnearly -60 degrees F. What seems\nto be its body is actually hollow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00479" index="479">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of plasma. It\nis known to infiltrate electronic\ndevices and wreak havoc.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00480" index="480">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known as “The Being of Knowledge.”\nIt is said that it can wipe out the\nmemory of those who see its eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00481" index="481">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known as “The Being of Emotion.”\nIt taught humans the nobility of\nsorrow, pain, and joy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00482" index="482">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known as “The Being of Willpower.”\nIt sleeps at the bottom of a lake\nto keep the world in balance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00483" index="483">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the power to control time.\nIt appears in Sinnoh-region myths\nas an ancient deity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00484" index="484">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the ability to distort\nspace. It is described as a deity\nin Sinnoh-region mythology.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00485" index="485">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It dwells in volcanic caves. It\ndigs in with its cross-shaped feet\nto crawl on ceilings and walls.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00486" index="486">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">There is an enduring legend that\nstates this Pokémon towed\ncontinents with ropes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00487" index="487">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that is said to live in a\nworld on the reverse side of ours.\nIt appears in an ancient cemetery.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00488" index="488">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Shiny particles are released from\nits wings like a veil. It is said\nto represent the crescent moon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00489" index="489">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that lives in warm seas.\nIt inflates the flotation sac on its\nhead to drift and search for food.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00490" index="490">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Born on a cold seafloor, it\nwill swim great distances to\nreturn to its birthplace.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00491" index="491">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can lull people to sleep and\nmake them dream. It is active\nduring nights of the new moon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00492" index="492">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in flower patches and\navoids detection by curling up\nto look like a flowering plant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_00493" index="493">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is described in mythology as\nthe Pokémon that shaped the\nuniverse with its 1,000 arms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_unused_494" index="494">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_unused_495" index="495">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_496" index="496">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An alien virus that fell to earth\non a meteor underwent a DNA\nmutation to become this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_497" index="497">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An alien virus that fell to earth\non a meteor underwent a DNA\nmutation to become this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_498" index="498">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An alien virus that fell to earth\non a meteor underwent a DNA\nmutation to become this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_499" index="499">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When BURMY evolved, its cloak\nbecame a part of this Pokémon’s\nbody. The cloak is never shed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_500" index="500">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When BURMY evolved, its cloak\nbecame a part of this Pokémon’s\nbody. The cloak is never shed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_501" index="501">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon that is said to live in a\nworld on the reverse side of ours.\nIt appears in an ancient cemetery.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_502" index="502">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in flower patches and\navoids detection by curling up\nto look like a flowering plant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_503" index="503">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of plasma. It\nis known to infiltrate electronic\ndevices and wreak havoc.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_504" index="504">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of plasma. It\nis known to infiltrate electronic\ndevices and wreak havoc.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_505" index="505">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of plasma. It\nis known to infiltrate electronic\ndevices and wreak havoc.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_506" index="506">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of plasma. It\nis known to infiltrate electronic\ndevices and wreak havoc.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_form_507" index="507">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of plasma. It\nis known to infiltrate electronic\ndevices and wreak havoc.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lillipup" index="508">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Though it is a very brave Pokémon,\nit’s also smart enough to check\nits foe’s strength and avoid battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_herdier" index="509">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very loyal Pokémon helps Trainers,\nand it also takes care of other Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_stoutland" index="510">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Being wrapped in its long fur is so\ncomfortable that a person would be fine\neven overnight on a wintry mountain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_purrloin" index="511">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their cute act is a ruse. They trick\npeople and steal their valuables\njust to see the looks on their faces.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_liepard" index="512">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their beautiful form comes from\nthe muscles they have developed.\nThey run silently in the night.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tympole" index="513">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By vibrating its cheeks, it emits\nsound waves imperceptible to humans\nand warns others of danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_palpitoad" index="514">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in the water and on land.\nIt uses its long, sticky tongue\nto immobilize its opponents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_seismitoad" index="515">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By putting power into its bumps,\nit creates vibrations and\nincreases the power of its punches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sewaddle" index="516">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Since this Pokémon makes its own clothes\nout of leaves, it is a popular mascot for\nfashion designers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_swadloon" index="517">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Preferring dark, damp places,\nit spends the entire day eating\nfallen leaves that lie around it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_leavanny" index="518">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Upon finding a small Pokémon, it weaves\nclothing for it from leaves by using\nthe sticky silk secreted from its mouth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_yamask" index="519">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon arose from the\nspirits of people interred in graves.\nEach retains memories of its former life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cofagrigus" index="520">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Grave robbers who mistake them\nfor real coffins and get too close\nend up trapped inside their bodies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_trubbish" index="521">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Wanting more garbage, they\nfollow people who litter.\nThey always belch poison gas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_garbodor" index="522">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Consuming garbage makes\nnew kinds of poison gases\nand liquids inside their bodies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_emolga" index="523">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It glides on its outstretched membrane\nwhile shocking foes with the electricity\nstored in the pouches on its cheeks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_karrablast" index="524">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For some reason they evolve when they\nreceive electrical energy while they\nare attacking Shelmet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_escavalier" index="525">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Wearing the shell covering they stole\nfrom Shelmet, they defend themselves\nand attack with two lances.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_foongus" index="526">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lures Pokémon with its pattern\nthat looks just like a Poké Ball\nthen releases poison spores.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_amoonguss" index="527">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It moves the caps on both arms\nand does a dance to lure prey.\nIt prefers damp places.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_joltik" index="528">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Since it can’t generate its own\nelectricity, it sticks onto large-bodied\nPokémon and absorbs static electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_galvantula" index="529">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It creates barriers from electrified\nsilk that stun foes. This works\nas a weapon as well as a defense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ferroseed" index="530">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It absorbs the iron it finds in\nthe rock while clinging to the ceiling.\nIt shoots spikes when in danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ferrothorn" index="531">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By swinging around its three\nspiky feelers and shooting spikes,\nit can obliterate an opponent.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_klink" index="532">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Two bodies comprise a fixed pair.\nThey spin around each\nother to generate energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_klang" index="533">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A minigear and big gear comprise its body.\nIf the minigear it launches at\na foe doesn’t return, it will die.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_klinklang" index="534">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The minigear spins at high speed. Then\nthe energy from the red core charges\nthe minigear to make it ready to fire.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_elgyem" index="535">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Rumors of its origin are\nlinked to a UFO crash site\nin the desert 50 years ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_beheeyem" index="536">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently, it communicates by\nflashing its three fingers, but\nthose patterns haven’t been decoded.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_litwick" index="537">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its flame is usually out, but it\nstarts shining when Litwick absorbs\nlife-force from people or Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lampent" index="538">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The spirits it absorbs fuel its baleful\nfire. It hangs around hospitals\nwaiting for people to pass on.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_chandelure" index="539">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The spirits burned up in its\nominous flame lose their way\nand wander this world forever.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_shelmet" index="540">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it and Karrablast are together, and\nboth receive electrical stimulation,\nthey both evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_accelgor" index="541">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its body dries out, it weakens.\nSo it wraps a membrane around itself\nfor protection while it spits poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bouffalant" index="542">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They are known to charge so wildly that\nif a train were to enter their territory,\nthey would send it flying.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bunnelby" index="543">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They use their large ears to dig\nburrows. They will dig the whole night\nthrough.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_diggersby" index="544">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As powerful as an excavator, its ears\ncan reduce dense bedrock to rubble.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fletchling" index="545">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it’s excited, its temperature can\ndouble, spiking hormone production in\nits body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fletchinder" index="546">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its speed right after takeoff already\nputs it in the top speed class of all\nbird Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_talonflame" index="547">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When attacking prey, it can reach\nspeeds of up to 310 mph. It finishes its\nprey off with a colossal kick.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_litleo" index="548">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The stronger the opponent it faces, the\nmore heat and power flow through its\nbody.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pyroar" index="549">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The male with the largest mane of fire\nis the leader of the pride.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_espurr" index="550">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The organ that emits its intense\npsychic power is sheltered by its ears\nto keep power from leaking out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_meowstic" index="551">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When in danger, it raises its ears and\nreleases enough psychic power to grind\na 10-ton truck to dust.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sylveon" index="552">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sends a soothing aura from its\nribbonlike feelers to calm fights.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dedenne" index="553">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its upper whiskers are sensors that\nsurvey its surroundings. Its lower\nwhiskers shoot electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_phantump" index="554">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is created when a spirit possesses\nrotten tree stumps. It prefers to live\nin abandoned forests.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_trevenant" index="555">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can control trees at will. It will\ntrap people who harm the forest, so they\ncan never leave.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pumpkaboo" index="556">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to carry wandering spirits\nto the place where they belong so they\ncan move on.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gourgeist" index="557">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It enwraps its prey in its hairlike\narms. It sings joyfully as it observes\nthe suffering of its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_noibat" index="558">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live in pitch black caves. Their\nenormous ears can emit ultrasonic waves\nof 200,000 hertz.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_noivern" index="559">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This hot-blooded Pokémon attacks\nanything it sees with ultrasonic waves\nthat can crush boulders.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_applin" index="560">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As soon as it’s born, it burrows into\nan apple. the flavor of the apple is\nwhat determines its evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_flapple" index="561">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It ate a sour apple, which induced its\nevolution. It stores an acid capable of\ncausing chemical burns in its cheeks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_appletun" index="562">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It ate a sweet apple, which induced\nits evolution. Back in the day, children\nused to have it as a snack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sizzlipede" index="563">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores flammable gas in its body\nand uses it to generate heat. It then\ncoils around its prey and cooks it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_centiskorch" index="564">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This excessively hostile Pokémon has\nlarge and very sharp fangs in addition\nto its dangerous burning body. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wyrdeer" index="565">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The fur shed from its beard retains\nheat well and is a highly useful\nmaterial for winter clothing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kleavor" index="566">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Parts of its body turned to stone when\nit evolved thanks to an extremely rare\nore found in volcanic areas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ursaluna" index="567">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">I believe it was Hisui’s swampy terrain\nthat gave Ursaluna its burly physique\nand newfound capacity to manipulate peat\nat will.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_annihilape" index="568">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its anger rose beyond a critical\npoint, this Pokémon gained power that is\nunfettered by the limits\nof its physical body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_farigiraf" index="569">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The hardened head from the tail protects\nthe head of the main body as\nFarigiraf whips its long neck\naround to headbutt enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dudunsparce" index="570">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It drives enemies out of its nest\nby sucking in enough air to fill its\nlong, narrow lungs, then releasing\nthe air in an intense blast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dipplin" index="571">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Dipplin is two creatures in one Pokémon.\nIts evolution was triggered by a special\napple grown only in one place.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hydrapple" index="572">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These capricious syrpents have banded\ntogether. On the rare occasion\nthat their moods align,\ntheir true power is unleashed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_slowpoke_galarian" index="573">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lazes vacantly near water.\nIf something bites its tail, it won’t\neven notice for a whole day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_slowbro_galarian" index="574">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If the tail-biting SHELLDER is thrown\noff in a harsh battle, it reverts to\nbeing an ordinary SLOWPOKE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_victini" index="575">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it shares the infinite energy\nit creates, that being’s entire body\nwill be overflowing with power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_snivy" index="576">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Being exposed to sunlight makes\nits movements swifter. It uses\nvines more adeptly than its hands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_servine" index="577">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it gets dirty, its leaves\ncan’t be used in photosynthesis,\nso it always keeps itself clean.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_serperior" index="578">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It only gives its all against\nstrong opponents who are not fazed\nby the glare from Serperior’s noble eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tepig" index="579">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves to eat roasted berries,\nbut sometimes it gets too excited\nand burns them to a crisp.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pignite" index="580">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The more it eats, the more fuel it has\nto make the fire in its stomach stronger.\nThis fills it with even more power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_emboar" index="581">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A flaring beard of fire is proof\nthat it is fired up. It is adept\nat using many different moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_oshawott" index="582">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The scalchop on its stomach isn’t\njust used for battle--it can be used\nto break open hard berries as well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dewott" index="583">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As a result of strict training,\neach Dewott learns different\nforms for using the scalchops.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_samurott" index="584">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In the time it takes a foe to blink,\nit can draw and sheathe the seamitars\nattached to its front legs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_patrat" index="585">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Extremely cautious, one of them\nwill always be on the lookout, but it\nwon’t notice a foe coming from behind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_watchog" index="586">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using luminescent matter,\nit makes its eyes and body glow\nand stuns attacking opponents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pansage" index="587">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s good at finding berries and\ngathers them from all over. It’s kind\nenough to share them with friends.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_simisage" index="588">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It strikes its enemies\nwith a thorn-covered tail.\nThe leaf on its head is bitter.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pansear" index="589">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Very intelligent, it roasts\nberries before eating them.\nIt likes to help people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_simisear" index="590">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it gets excited, embers rise\nfrom its head and tail and it gets hot.\nFor some reason, it loves sweets.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_panpour" index="591">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The water stored inside the tuft\non its head is full of nutrients.\nIt waters plants with it using its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_simipour" index="592">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It prefers places with clean water.\nWhen its tuft runs low, it replenishes\nit by siphoning up water with its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_munna" index="593">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon appears before people and\nPokémon who are having nightmares and\neats those dreams.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_musharna" index="594">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The dream mist coming from its forehead\nchanges into many different colors\ndepending on the dream that was eaten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pidove" index="595">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very forgetful Pokémon will\nwait for a new order from its Trainer\neven though it already has one.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tranquill" index="596">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">No matter where in the world it goes,\nit knows where its nest is, so it never\ngets separated from its Trainer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_unfezant" index="597">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Males swing the plumage on\ntheir heads to threaten others,\nbut females are better at flying.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_blitzle" index="598">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its mane shines when it discharges\nelectricity. They use the frequency and\nrhythm of these flashes to communicate.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zebstrika" index="599">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When this ill-tempered Pokémon\nruns wild, it shoots lightning\nfrom its mane in all directions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_roggenrola" index="600">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The hexagonal-shaped hole is its ear.\nIt has a tendency to walk in the\ndirection the sound is coming from.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_boldore" index="601">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it is healthy, its core sticks out.\nAlways facing the same way, it swiftly\nmoves front to back and left to right.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gigalith" index="602">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The solar rays it absorbs are\nprocessed in its energy core\nand fired as a ball of light.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_woobat" index="603">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The heart-shaped mark left on a body\nafter a Woobat has been attached\nto it is said to bring good fortune.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_swoobat" index="604">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shakes its tail vigorously when it\nemits ultrasonic waves strong enough\nto reduce concrete to rubble.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_drilbur" index="605">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By spinning its body, it can dig\nstraight through the ground\nat a speed of 30 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_excadrill" index="606">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Forming a drill with its steel claws\nand head, it can bore through a steel\nplate, no matter how thick it is.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_audino" index="607">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using the feelers on its ears,\nit can tell how someone is feeling\nor when an egg might hatch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_timburr" index="608">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Always carrying squared logs,\nthey help out with construction.\nAs they grow, they carry bigger logs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gurdurr" index="609">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With strengthened bodies,\nthey skillfully wield steel\nbeams to take down buildings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_conkeldurr" index="610">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Rather than rely on force,\nthey master moves that utilize the\ncentrifugal force of spinning concrete.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_throh" index="611">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it encounters a foe bigger\nthan itself, it wants to throw it.\nIt changes belts as it gets stronger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sawk" index="612">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Desiring the strongest karate chop,\nthey seclude themselves in mountains\nand train without sleeping.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_venipede" index="613">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using the feelers on its head and tail,\nit picks up vibrations in the air to\ndetermine its prey’s location and state.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_whirlipede" index="614">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Storing energy for evolution, it sits.\nBut, when predators approach, it moves\nto stab them with poison spikes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_scolipede" index="615">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It clasps its prey with the claws\non its neck until it stops moving.\nThen it finishes it off with deadly poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cottonee" index="616">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Perhaps because they feel more at ease\nin a group, they stick to others they\nfind. They end up looking like a cloud.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_whimsicott" index="617">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They appear along with whirlwinds. They\npull pranks, such as moving furniture\nand leaving balls of cotton in homes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_petilil" index="618">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The leaves on its head grow right back\neven if they fall out. These bitter leaves\nrefresh those who eat them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lilligant" index="619">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The fragrance of the garland\non its head has a relaxing effect,\nbut taking care of it is very difficult.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_basculin" index="620">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Red- and blue-striped Basculin are\nvery violent and always fighting.\nThey are also remarkably tasty.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sandile" index="621">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live hidden under hot desert sands\nin order to keep their body temperature\nfrom dropping.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_krokorok" index="622">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Protected by thin membranes, their\neyes can see even in the dead of night.\nThey live in groups of a few individuals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_krookodile" index="623">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Very violent Pokémon, they try\nto clamp down on anything that\nmoves in front of their eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_darumaka" index="624">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it sleeps, it pulls its limbs\ninto its body and its internal fire\ngoes down to 1,100 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_darmanitan" index="625">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its internal fire burns at 2,500 degrees\nFahrenheit, making enough power that it\ncan destroy a dump truck with one punch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_maractus" index="626">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it moves rhythmically, it\nmakes a sound similar to maracas,\nmaking the surprised Pokémon flee.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dwebble" index="627">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it finds a stone of a suitable size,\nit secretes a liquid from its mouth\nto open up a hole to crawl into.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_crustle" index="628">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its boulder is broken in\nbattles for territory, it feels\nunsure and begins to weaken.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_scraggy" index="629">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Proud of its sturdy skull, it\nsuddenly headbutts everything,\nbut its weight makes it unstable, too.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_scrafty" index="630">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It pulls up its shed skin to protect\nitself while it kicks. The bigger\nthe crest, the more respected it is.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sigilyph" index="631">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The guardians of an ancient city,\nthey always fly the same route\nwhile keeping watch for invaders.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tirtouga" index="632">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon was restored from a fossil.\nIt swam skillfully and dove\nto depths beyond half a mile.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_carracosta" index="633">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It could knock out a foe with a slap from\none of its developed front appendages\nand chew it up, shell or bones and all.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_archen" index="634">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was revived from an ancient fossil.\nNot able to fly, it lived in treetops\nand hopped from one branch to another.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_archeops" index="635">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It runs better than it flies.\nIt takes off into the sky by\nrunning at a speed of 25 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zorua" index="636">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It changes so it looks just like its foe,\ntricks it, and then uses that opportunity\nto flee.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zoroark" index="637">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Stories say those who tried to catch\nZoroark were trapped in an illusion\nand punished.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_minccino" index="638">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Minccino greet each other\nby grooming one another\nthoroughly with their tails.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cinccino" index="639">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Cinccino’s body is coated in a\nspecial oil that helps it deflect\nattacks, such as punches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gothita" index="640">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stares intently at everything.\nIt can become so obsessed with watching\nthat it doesn’t notice attacks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gothorita" index="641">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">According to many old tales, it creates\nfriends for itself by controlling sleeping\nchildren on starry nights.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gothitelle" index="642">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can see the future from the movement\nof the stars. When it learns its Trainer’s\nlife span, it cries in sadness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_solosis" index="643">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because their bodies are enveloped in\na special liquid, they are fine in any\nenvironment, no matter how severe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_duosion" index="644">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When their two divided brains think the\nsame thoughts, their psychic power is\nmaximized.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_reuniclus" index="645">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They use psychic power to control their\narms, which are made of a special liquid.\nThey can crush boulders psychically.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ducklett" index="646">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They are better at swimming than flying,\nand they happily eat their favorite food,\npeat moss, as they dive underwater.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_swanna" index="647">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Despite their elegant appearance,\nthey can flap their wings strongly\nand fly for thousands of miles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vanillite" index="648">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Theoretically, this Pokémon formed from\nicicles bathed in energy from the morning\nsun. Their breath is\n-58 degrees Farenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vanillish" index="649">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They cool down the surrounding air\nand create ice particles, which\nthey use to freeze their foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vanilluxe" index="650">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Swallowing large amounts of water, they\nmake snow clouds inside their bodies and,\nwhen angry, cause violent blizzards.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_deerling" index="651">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their coloring changes according to the\nseasons and can be slightly affected\nby the temperature and humidity as well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sawsbuck" index="652">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They migrate according to the seasons,\nso some people call Sawsbuck the\nharbingers of spring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_frillish" index="653">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its veil-like arms stun and wrap\na foe, that foe will be dragged miles\nbelow the surface, never to return.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_jellicent" index="654">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is mostly seawater.\nIt’s said there’s a castle of ships\nJellicent have sunk on the seafloor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_alomomola" index="655">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gently holds injured\nand weak Pokémon in its fins.\nIts special membrane heals their wounds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tynamo" index="656">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One alone can emit only a trickle of\nelectricity, so a group of them gathers\nto unleash a powerful electric shock.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_eelektrik" index="657">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wraps itself around its prey and\nparalyzes it with electricity from the\nround spots on its sides. Then it chomps.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_eelektross" index="658">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It latches on to prey with its sucker\nmouth, sinking in its fangs and shocking\nthe prey with powerful electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_axew" index="659">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its large tusks have a tendency to\nbreak, but each time they grow back,\nthey grow in harder and sturdier.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fraxure" index="660">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A broken tusk will not grow back,\nso it diligently sharpens its tusks on\nriver rocks after the end of a battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_haxorus" index="661">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its tusks are incredibly destructive.\nThey can easily slice through a thick,\nsturdy steel column every time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cubchoo" index="662">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their snot is a barometer of health.\nWhen healthy, their snot is sticky and\nthe power of their ice moves increases.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_beartic" index="663">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They love the cold seas of the north.\nThey create pathways across the ocean\nwaters by freezing their own breath.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cryogonal" index="664">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They are composed of ice crystals. They\ncapture prey with chains of ice, freezing\nthe prey at -148 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_stunfisk" index="665">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its opponent can’t be paralyzed,\nit contorts itself with unexpected speed\nand flops away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mienfoo" index="666">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It takes pride in the speed at which it\ncan use moves. What it loses in power,\nit makes up for in quantity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mienshao" index="667">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using the long fur on its arms like whips,\nit launches into combo attacks that,\nonce started, no one can stop.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_druddigon" index="668">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It runs through the narrow tunnels\nformed by Excadrill and Onix.\nIt uses its sharp claws to catch prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_golett" index="669">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ancient science fashioned\nthis Pokémon from clay.\nIt’s been active for thousands of years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_golurk" index="670">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Golurk were created to protect\npeople and Pokémon.\nThey run on a mysterious energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pawniard" index="671">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ignoring their injuries, groups attack\nby sinking the blades that cover\ntheir bodies into their prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bisharp" index="672">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This pitiless Pokémon commands a group\nof Pawniard to hound prey into immobility.\nIt then moves in to finish the prey off.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rufflet" index="673">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stands up to massive opponents, not\nout of courage, but out of recklessness.\nBut that is how it gets stronger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_braviary" index="674">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For the sake of its friends, this\nbrave warrior of the sky will not\nstop battling, even if injured.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vullaby" index="675">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their wings are too tiny to allow them\nto fly. They guard their posteriors with\nbones that were gathered by Mandibuzz.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mandibuzz" index="676">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They fly in circles around the sky.\nWhen they spot prey, they attack and\ncarry it back to their nest with ease.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_heatmor" index="677">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It draws in air through its tail,\ntransforms it into fire, and uses it like\na tongue. It melts Durant and eats them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_durant" index="678">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Individuals each play different roles in\ndriving Heatmor, their natural predator,\naway from their colony.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_deino" index="679">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Lacking sight, it’s unaware of its\nsurroundings, so it bumps into\nthings and eats anything that moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zweilous" index="680">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The two heads do not get along.\nWhichever head eats more than\nthe other gets to be the leader.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hydreigon" index="681">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It responds to movement by attacking.\nThis scary, three-headed Pokémon\ndevours everything in its path!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_larvesta" index="682">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Said to have been born from the sun,\nit spews fire from its horns and encases\nitself in a cocoon of fire when it evolves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_volcarona" index="683">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Thought to be an embodiment of the sun,\nit appeared during a bitterly cold winter\nand saved Pokémon from freezing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cobalion" index="684">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a body and heart of steel.\nIt worked with its allies to punish\npeople when they hurt Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_terrakion" index="685">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Spoken of in legend, this Pokémon\nused its phenomenal power to destroy a\ncastle in its effort to protect Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_virizion" index="686">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Legends say this Pokémon\nconfounded opponents\nwith its swift movements.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tornadus" index="687">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In every direction it flies,\ncreating winds so powerful,\nthey blow everything away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_thundurus" index="688">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it flies around, it shoots lightning all\nover the place and causes forest fires.\nIt is therefore disliked.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_reshiram" index="689">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary Pokémon can scorch\nthe world with fire. It helps those\nwho want to build a world of truth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zekrom" index="690">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary Pokémon can scorch\nthe world with lightning. It assists those\nwho want to build an ideal world.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_landorus" index="691">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">From the forces of lightning and wind,\nit creates energy to give nutrients\nto the soil and make the land abundant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kyurem" index="692">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary ice Pokémon waits for\na hero to fill in the missing parts\nof its body with truth or ideals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_keldeo" index="693">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it is resolute, its body fills\nwith power and it becomes swifter.\nIts jumps are then too fast to follow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_meloetta" index="694">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The melodies sung by Meloetta\nhave the power to make Pokémon\nthat hear them happy or sad.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_genesect" index="695">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon existed 300 million\nyears ago. Team Plasma altered it\nand attached a cannon to its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_chespin" index="696">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Such a thick shell of wood covers its\nhead and back that even a direct hit\nfrom a truck wouldn’t faze it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_quilladin" index="697">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It relies on its sturdy shell to\ndeflect predators’ attacks. It\ncounterattacks with its sharp quills.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_chesnaught" index="698">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it takes a defensive posture with\nits fists guarding its face, it could\nwithstand a bomb blast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fennekin" index="699">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Eating a twig fills it with energy, and\nits roomy ears give vent to very hot\nair.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_braixen" index="700">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With friction from its tail fur, it\nsets the twig on its tail on fire and\nlaunches into battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_delphox" index="701">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gazes into the flame at its branch\nto achieve a focused state, allowing it\nto see the future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_froakie" index="702">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It secretes bubbles from its chest and\nback. The bubbles reduce the damage it\nwould take when attacked.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_frogadier" index="703">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can\nscale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in\na minute’s time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_greninja" index="704">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It creates throwing stars out of\ncompressed water, that can split metal\nin two.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_scatterbug" index="705">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The powder that covers its body\nregulates its temperature, so it can\nlive in any region or climate.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_spewpa" index="706">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The beaks of birds can’t begin to\nscratch its stalwart body. To defend\nitself, it spews powder.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vivillon" index="707">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The colorful patterns on this Pokémon’s\nwings depend on the climate and\ntopography of its habitat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_flabebe" index="708">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It draws and controls the hidden power\nof flowers. The flower it holds is most\nlikely part of its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_floette" index="709">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the flowers of a well-tended\nflower bed bloom, it appears and\ncelebrates with an elegant dance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_florges" index="710">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its life can span several hundred\nyears. It’s said to devote its entire\nlife to protecting gardens.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_skiddo" index="711">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Thought to be one of the first Pokémon\nto live in harmony with humans, it has\na placid disposition.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gogoat" index="712">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They inhabit mountainous regions. The\nleader of the herd is decided by a\nbattle of clashing horns.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pancham" index="713">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grows up imitating the behavior of\nPangoro, which it looks up to as a\nleader.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pangoro" index="714">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon boasts great physical\nstrength. Many Trainers are also smitten\nby its lively character.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_furfrou" index="715">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Historically, in the Kalos region,\nthese Pokémon were the designated\nguardians of the king.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_honedge" index="716">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is born when a departed spirit\ninhabits a sword. It attaches to people\nand drinks their life force.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_doublade" index="717">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The complex attack patterns of its two\nswords are unstoppable, even for an\naccomplished opponent.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_aegislash" index="718">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can detect the innate qualities of\nleadership. Whoever it recognizes is\ndestined to become king.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_spritzee" index="719">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It emits a scent that delights those\nwho smell it. The fragrance changes\ndepending on what it has eaten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_aromatisse" index="720">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It devises various scents and emits\nscents that its enemies dislike in order\nto gain an edge in battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_swirlix" index="721">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it eats nothing but sweets, its\nfur is as sticky sweet as cotton\ncandy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_slurpuff" index="722">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can distinguish the faintest of\nscents. It puts its sense of smell to\nuse by helping pastry chefs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_inkay" index="723">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It draws prey near with its blinking\nlights and then wraps them up in its\nlong tentacles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_malamar" index="724">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wields the most compelling hypnotic\npowers of any Pokémon, and it forces\nothers to do anything.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_binacle" index="725">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Two Binacle live together on one rock.\nWhen they fight, one of them will move\nto a different rock.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_barbaracle" index="726">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When they evolve, two Binacle multiply\ninto seven. They fight with the power\nof seven Binacle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_skrelp" index="727">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It looks just like rotten kelp. It\nhides from foes while storing up power\nfor its evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dragalge" index="728">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Tales are told of ships that wander\ninto seas where Dragalge live, never to\nreturn.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_clauncher" index="729">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They knock down flying prey by firing\ncompressed water from their massive\nclaws like shooting a pistol.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_clawitzer" index="730">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their enormous claws launch cannonballs\nof water powerful enough to pierce\ntanker hulls.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_helioptile" index="731">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The frills on either side of its head\nhave cells that generate electricity\nwhen exposed to sunlight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_heliolisk" index="732">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flares its frill and generates\nenergy. It can generate sufficient\nelectricity to power a skyscraper.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tyrunt" index="733">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its immense jaws have enough destructive\nforce to chew up an automobile. It lived\n100 million years ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tyrantrum" index="734">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Nothing could stop this Pokémon 100\nmillion years ago, so it behaved like a\nking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_amaura" index="735">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This calm Pokémon lived in a cold land\nwhere there were no violent predators\nlike Tyrantrum.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_aurorus" index="736">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This usually quiet and kindly\nPokémon has a surface temperature\nof around -240 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hawlucha" index="737">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although its body is small, its\nproficient fighting skills enable it to\nkeep up with big bruisers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_carbink" index="738">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Born from temperatures and pressures\ndeep underground, it fires beams from\nthe stone in its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_goomy" index="739">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s covered in a slimy membrane that\nmakes any punches or kicks slide off it\nharmlessly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sliggoo" index="740">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crawls along sluggishly. The swirly\nprotrusion on its back is filled with\nits brain and other organs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_goodra" index="741">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An amazingly friendly Pokémon, but if\nleft to itself, loneliness overcomes it,\nand it oozes gooey tears.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_klefki" index="742">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These key collectors threaten any\nattackers by fiercely jingling their\nkeys at them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bergmite" index="743">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It blocks opponents’ attacks with the\nice that shields its body. It uses cold\nair to repair any crack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_avalugg" index="744">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The way several Bergmite huddle on its\nback make it look like an aircraft\ncarrier made of ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_xerneas" index="745">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the horns on its head shine in\nseven different colors, it is said to be\nsharing everlasting life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_yveltal" index="746">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its life comes to an end, it\nabsorbs the life energy of every living\nthing and turns into a cocoon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zygarde" index="747">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the Kalos region’s ecosystem falls\ninto disarray, it appears and reveals\nits secret power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_diancie" index="748">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can instantly create many diamonds\nby compressing the carbon in the air\nbetween its hands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hoopa" index="749">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gathers things it likes and passes\nthem through its loop to teleport them\nto a secret place.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_volcanion" index="750">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It expels its internal steam from the\narms on its back. It has enough power to\nblow away a mountain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rowlet" index="751">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It feels relaxed in tight, dark places\nand has been known to use its Trainer’s\npocket or bag as a nest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dartrix" index="752">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It throws sharp feathers called blade\nquills at enemies or prey. It seldom\nmisses.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_decidueye" index="753">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although basically cool and cautious,\nwhen it’s caught by surprise, it’s\nseized by panic.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_litten" index="754">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It doesn’t allow its emotions to be\neasily seen. Earning its trust takes\ntime. It prefers solitude.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_torracat" index="755">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It boasts powerful front legs. With a\nsingle punch, it can bend an iron bar\nright over.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_incineroar" index="756">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its fighting spirit is set alight,\nthe flames around its waist become\nespecially intense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_popplio" index="757">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The balloons it inflates with its nose\ngrow larger and larger as it practices\nday by day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_brionne" index="758">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks by smacking its enemies with\nthe exploding water balloons that it\ncreates.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_primarina" index="759">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To Primarina, every battle is a stage.\nIt takes down its prey with beautiful\nsinging and dancing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikipek" index="760">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It may look spindly, but its neck\nmuscles are heavy-duty. It can peck at a\ntree 16 times per second!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_trumbeak" index="761">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can bend the tip of its beak to\nproduce over a hundred different cries\nat will.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_toucannon" index="762">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known for forming harmonious couples,\nit is brought to wedding ceremonies as a\ngood luck charm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_yungoos" index="763">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It prefers to eat fresh living things\nso it marches down streets in search of\nprey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gumshoos" index="764">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Patient by nature, it loses control of\nitself and pounces when it spots its\nfavorite meal-Rattata!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_grubbin" index="765">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its strong jaw enables it to scrape\ntrees and slurp out the sap. It normally\nlives underground.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_charjabug" index="766">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">From the food it digests, it generates\nelectricity, and it stores this energy\nin its electric sac.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vikavolt" index="767">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flusters opponents with acrobatic\nflying maneuvers. This creates an\nopening for it to attack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_crabrawler" index="768">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its hard pincers are well suited to\nboth offense and defense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_crabominable" index="769">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores coldness in its pincers and\npummels its foes. It can even smash\nthick walls of ice to bits!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_oricorio" index="770">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Oricorio has sipped red nectar. Its\npassionate dance moves cause its enemies\nto combust in both body and mind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cutiefly" index="771">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Myriads of Cutiefly flutter above the\nheads of people who have auras\nresembling those of flowers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ribombee" index="772">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Some of Ribombee’s pollen puffs are\nhighly nutritious. They are sometimes\nsold as supplements.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rockruff" index="773">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it rubs the rocks on its neck\nagainst you, that’s proof of its love\nfor you.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lycanroc" index="774">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Well equipped with claws and fangs, it\nuses the sharp rocks in its mane as\nweapons.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wishiwashi" index="775">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They’re weak, so they move in schools.\nHowever, they can also often be seen all\nalone, having strayed from the school.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mareanie" index="776">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Aside from its head, its body parts\nregenerate quickly if they’re cut off.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_toxapex" index="777">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crawls along the ocean floor on its\n12 legs. It leaves a trail of Corsola\nbits scattered in its wake.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mudbray" index="778">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The mud stuck to Mudbray’s hooves\nenhances its grip and its powerful\nrunning gait.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mudsdale" index="779">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can trudge mountain roads without\nrest for three days, all the while\ndragging a 10-ton load.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dewpider" index="780">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crawls onto the land in search of\nfood. Its water bubble allows it to\nbreathe and protects its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_araquanid" index="781">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It delivers headbutts with the bubble\non its head. Small Pokémon get sucked\ninto it, where they drown.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fomantis" index="782">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves the sunshine. When it basks in\nthe sunlight regularly, it grows up\nwith vivid coloration.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lurantis" index="783">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For self-protection, it pretends to be\na bug Pokémon. Both of its arms bear\nkeen-edged petals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_morelull" index="784">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It scatters spores that flicker and\nglow. Anyone seeing these lights falls\ninto a deep slumber.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_shiinotic" index="785">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it starts fighting for territory\nwith Parasect, the entire area gets\ncompletely coated in spores!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_salandit" index="786">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It burns its bodily fluids to create a\npoisonous gas. It weakens enemies and\nsends them reeling with it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_salazzle" index="787">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It punishes Salandit that couldn’t\nbring it food with a fierce slap of its\nflame-spewing palm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_stufful" index="788">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Stufful hates to be hugged or touched\nin any way. It will squirm, thrash, and\nresist with amazing power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bewear" index="789">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It boasts tremendous physical strength.\nMany people call it the most dangerous\nPokémon in Alola region.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bounsweet" index="790">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because of its sweet, delicious aroma,\nbird Pokémon are always after it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_steenee" index="791">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bounces around, swinging the sepals\non its head with abandon. It’s quite\npainful when it smacks you!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tsareena" index="792">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A master of grand and beautiful kicks,\nit can knock out even kickboxing\nchampions with a single blow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_comfey" index="793">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Baths prepared with the flowers from\nits vine have a relaxing effect so it is\na hit to many people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_oranguru" index="794">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known for its extreme intelligence, it\nwill look down on inexperienced\nTrainers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_passimian" index="795">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They form groups of 20 individuals.\nTheir mutual bond is remarkable-they\nwill never let down a comrade.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wimpod" index="796">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An astonishingly coward Pokémon, it\nwhirs its legs at high speed to run away\nif anything comes near it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_golisopod" index="797">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With a flashing slash of its giant\nsharp claws, it cleaves seawater-or even\nair-right in two.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sandygast" index="798">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Born from a sand mound playfully built\nby a child, this Pokémon embodies the\ngrudges of the departed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_palossand" index="799">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Buried beneath the castle are masses of\ndried-up bones from those whose\nvitality it has drained.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pyukumuku" index="800">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is covered with slime. If you\naccidentally step on it, you’ll slip,\nand it will get mad at you!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_type_null" index="801">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">There’s danger of its going on a\nrampage, so its true power is sealed\naway beneath its control mask.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_silvally" index="802">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It destroyed its own control mask. It\nhas become capable of changing type by\nequipping special memories.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_minior" index="803">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats dust in the atmosphere. The\ncomposition of the dust determines the\ncolor of its core.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_komala" index="804">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stays asleep from the moment it’s\nborn. When it falls into a deep sleep,\nit stops moving altogether.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_turtonator" index="805">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gushes fire and poisonous gases from\nits nostrils. Its dung is an explosive\nsubstance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_togedemaru" index="806">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it’s surprised or agitated, the 14\nfur spikes on its back will stand up\ninvoluntarily.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mimikyu" index="807">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It conceals its terrifying appearance\nbeneath an old rag so it can get closer\nto people and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bruxish" index="808">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its skin is thick enough to fend off\nspikes. With its robust teeth, it\ncrunches up and eats the spikes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_drampa" index="809">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It appears in towns and plays with the\nchildren. Drampa will protect kids when\nthey’re in danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dhelmise" index="810">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wraps its prey in green seaweed and\nsucks away their vitality. It only\nlikes to go after big prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_jangmo_o" index="811">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live in mountains where no trace\nof humans can be detected. It grows as\nit battles others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hakamo_o" index="812">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It leaps at its prey with a courageous\nshout. Its scaly punches tear its\nopponents to shreds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kommo_o" index="813">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It battles valiantly with its fists,\nwhich are armored in steel scales.\nKommo-o specializes in uppercuts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tapu_koko" index="814">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This guardian deity of Melemele summons\nthunderclouds and stores their\nlightning inside its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tapu_lele" index="815">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This guardian deity of Akala is\nguilelessly cruel. Its flowers’ fragrant\naroma is its source of energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tapu_bulu" index="816">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The guardian deity of Ula’ula is a lazy\nPokémon. It commands plants to\nimmobilize its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tapu_fini" index="817">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The guardian deity of Poni can control\nwater. It can create pure water that\nwill wash away any impurity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cosmog" index="818">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is gaseous and frail. It\nslowly grows as it collects dust from\nthe atmosphere.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cosmoem" index="819">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it absorbs light, Cosmoem continues\nto grow. Its golden shell is\nsurprisingly solid.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_solgaleo" index="820">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In writings from the distant past, it’s\ncalled by the name ’the beast that\ndevours the sun.’.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lunala" index="821">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sometimes summons unknown powers and\nlife-forms to this world from holes\nthat lead to other worlds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_nihilego" index="822">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A life-form from another world, it was\ndubbed a UB and is thought to produce a\nstrong neurotoxin.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_buzzwole" index="823">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Buzzwole goes around showing off its\nabnormally swollen muscles. It is one\nkind of Ultra Beast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pheromosa" index="824">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One of the dangerous Ultra Beasts, it\nhas been spotted running across the land\nat terrific speeds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_xurkitree" index="825">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. It\nraided a power plant, so it energizes\nitself with electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_celesteela" index="826">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole.\nWitnesses observed it flying across the\nsky at high speed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kartana" index="827">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Ultra Beast’s body, which is as\nthin as paper, is like a sharpened\nsword.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_guzzlord" index="828">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An unknown life-form called a UB. It\nmay be constantly hungry-it is certainly\nalways devouring something.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_necrozma" index="829">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Light is the source of its energy. If\nit isn’t devouring light, impurities\nbuild up in it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_magearna" index="830">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its mechanized body is merely a vessel.\nIts true self is its Soul-Heart, an\nartificial soul.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_marshadow" index="831">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lurks in the shadows of others,\ncopying their movements and powers. It\nis craven and cowering.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_poipole" index="832">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Ultra Beast is well enough liked\nto be chosen as a first partner in its\nown world.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_naganadel" index="833">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores hundreds of liters of\npoisonous liquid in its body. It is one\nof the organisms known as UBs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_stakataka" index="834">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When stone walls started moving and\nattacking, the brute’s true identity was\nthis mysterious life-form.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_blacephalon" index="835">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It causes explosions, then takes\nadvantage of opponents’ surprise to rob\nthem of their vitality.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zeraora" index="836">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It approaches its enemies at the speed\nof lightning, then tears them limb from\nlimb with its sharp claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_meltan" index="837">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It melts particles of iron and other\nmetals found in the subsoil, so it can\nabsorb theminto its body of molten steel.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_melmetal" index="838">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Revered long ago for its capacity to\ncreate iron from nothing, for\nsome reason it has come back\nto life after 3,000 years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_grookey" index="839">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks with rapid beats of its\nstick. As it strikes with amazing speed,\nit gets more and more pumped.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_thwackey" index="840">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The faster a Thwackey can beat out\na rhythm with its two sticks, the\nmore respect it wins from its peers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rillaboom" index="841">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By drumming, it taps into the power of\nits special tree stump. The roots of the\nstump follow its direction in battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_scorbunny" index="842">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has special pads on the backs of\nits feet, and one on its nose. Its\npads radiate tremendous heat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_raboot" index="843">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its thick and fluffy fur protects it\nfrom the cold and enables it to\nuse hotter fire moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cinderace" index="844">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gets pumped up when cheered on.\nBut if it starts showboating, it could put\nitself in a tough spot.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sobble" index="845">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it gets wet, its skin changes\ncolor, and this Pokémon becomes\ninvisible as if it were camouflaged.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_drizzile" index="846">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Highly intelligent but also very lazy,\nit keeps enemies out of its territory\nby laying traps everywhere.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_inteleon" index="847">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It picks out foes’ weak points so it\ncan precisely blast them with water\nthat shoots from its fingertips.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_skwovet" index="848">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon becomes uneasy if its\ncheeks are ever completely empty\nof berries.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_greedent" index="849">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon has strong teeth and\ncan chew through the toughest of\nberry shells.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rookidee" index="850">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It will bravely challenge any foe, no\nmatter how powerful. Even suffering\na defeat increases its strength a bit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_corvisquire" index="851">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The lessons of many harsh battles\nhave taught it how to accurately judge\nan opponent’s strength.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_corviknight" index="852">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The black luster of its steel body\ncould drive terror into the heart of\nany foe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_blipbug" index="853">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A constant collector of information,\nthis Pokémon is very smart. Very\nstrong is what it isn’t.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dottler" index="854">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it grows inside its shell, it uses\nits psychic abilities to monitor its\nsurroundings and wait for evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_orbeetle" index="855">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s famous for its high intelligence,\nand the large size of its brain is proof\nthat it has immense psychic power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_nickit" index="856">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Aided by the soft pads on its feet, it\nsilently raids the food stores of others.\nIt survives off its ill-gotten gains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_thievul" index="857">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With a lithe body and sharp claws, it\ngoes around stealing food and eggs.\nIt secretly marks its future targets.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gossifleur" index="858">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It anchors itself in the ground and\nbasks in the sun. After absorbing\nenough sunlight, it blooms vividly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_eldegoss" index="859">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The seeds attached to its cotton fluff\nare full of nutrients. It spreads them on\nthe wind so that others can benefit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wooloo" index="860">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its fleece grows too long, it won’t\nbe able to move. Cloth made with\nits wool is surprisingly durable.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dubwool" index="861">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its majestic horns are meant only to\nimpress the opposite gender. They\nnever see use in battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_chewtle" index="862">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently the itch of its teething\nimpels it to snap its jaws at anything\nin front of it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_drednaw" index="863">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With jaws that can shear through steel\nrods, this highly aggressive Pokémon\nchomps down on its unfortunate prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_yamper" index="864">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This greedy Pokémon only helps people\nwith their work because it wants treats.\nAs it runs, it crackles with electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_boltund" index="865">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sends electricity through its legs\nto boost their strength. Running at\ntop speed, it easily breaks 50 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rolycoly" index="866">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can race around like a unicycle,\neven on rough, rocky terrain. Burning\ncoal sustains it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_carkol" index="867">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By rapidly rolling its legs, it can\neasily travel at over 18 mph. It\nforms coal inside its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_coalossal" index="868">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">While engaged in battle, its mountain\nof coal will burn bright red, scorching\nthe surrounding area with sparks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_silicobra" index="869">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It spews sand from its nostrils. While\nthe enemy is blinded, it burrows into\nthe ground to hide.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sandaconda" index="870">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it contracts its body, over 220\npounds of sand sprays from its nose.\nIt becomes disheartened if it runs out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cramorant" index="871">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This hungry Pokémon swallows Arrokuda\nwhole. Occasionally, it makes a mistake\nand tries to swallow other Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_arrokuda" index="872">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It becomes extremely sluggish after\neating its fill. That’s when Cramorant\nswallows it up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_barraskewda" index="873">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its jaw that’s as sharp as a spear and\nas strong as steel. It spins its tail fins\nto surge forward at over 100 knots.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_toxel" index="874">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It manipulates the chemical makeup of\nits poison to produce electricity. Despite\na weak voltage, it can cause paralysis.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_toxtricity" index="875">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This short-tempered and aggressive\nPokémon chugs stagnant water to\nabsorb any toxins it might contain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_clobbopus" index="876">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s very curious, but its means of\ninvestigating things is to try to punch\nthem with its tentacles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_grapploct" index="877">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Searching for an opponent to test its\nskills against, it emerges onto land. Once\nthe battle is over, it\nreturns to the sea.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sinistea" index="878">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is said to have been\nborn when a lonely spirit possessed\na cold, leftover cup of tea.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_polteageist" index="879">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This species lives in antique teapots.\nMost pots are forgeries, but on rare\noccasions, an authentic work is found.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hatenna" index="880">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Via the protrusion on its head, it\nsenses other creatures’ emotions.\nIt prefers areas without people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hattrem" index="881">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">No matter who you are, if you bring\nstrong emotions near this Pokémon,\nit will silence you violently.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_hatterene" index="882">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known as the Forest Witch, if you are\ntoo loud around it, you risk being torn\napart by the claws on its tentacle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_impidimp" index="883">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sneaks into people’s homes, taking\nand feasting on the negative energy\nof the frustrated occupants.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_morgrem" index="884">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With sly cunning, it lures people into\nthe woods. Some believe it to have\nthe power to make crops grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_grimmsnarl" index="885">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its hairs work like muscle fibers.\nWhen its hairs unfurl, they latch on to\nfoes, ensnaring them like tentacles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_obstagoon" index="886">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It evolved after experiencing numerous\nfights. While crossing\nits arms, it lets out a\nshout that would make anyone flinch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_perrserker" index="887">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">What appears to be an iron helmet is\nactually hardened hair. This Pokémon\nlives for the thrill of battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cursola" index="888">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Be cautious of the ectoplasmic body\nsurrounding its soul. You’ll become stiff\nas stone if you touch it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sirfetchd" index="889">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">After deflecting attacks with its hard\nleaf shield, it strikes back with its sharp\nleek stalk. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mr_rime" index="890">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its amusing movements make it very\npopular. It releases its psychic power\nfrom the pattern on its belly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_runerigus" index="891">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Never touch its shadowlike body, or\nyou’ll be shown the horrific memories\nbehind the picture carved into it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_milcery" index="892">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They say that any patisserie visited\nby Milcery is guaranteed success and\ngood fortune.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_alcremie" index="893">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It evolved from a Milcery that held\nonto a Strawberry Sweet. Its flavor\ndepends on how it was mixed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_falinks" index="894">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The six of them work together as one.\nTeamwork is also their\nbattle strategy, and\nthey constantly change their formation.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pincurchin" index="895">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It feeds on seaweed, using its teeth\nto scrape it off rocks. Electric current\nflows from the tips of its spines.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_snom" index="896">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats snow that piles up on the\nground. The more snow it eats, the\nbigger its spikes grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_frosmoth" index="897">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Icy scales fall from its wings\nlike snow as it flies over fields\nand mountains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_stonjourner" index="898">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once a year, on a specific date and\nat a specific time, they gather out of\nnowhere and form up in a circle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_eiscue" index="899">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It drifted in on the flow of ocean\nwaters from a frigid place. It keeps its\nhead iced constantly to stay cold.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_indeedee" index="900">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Through its horns, it can pick up on the\nemotions of creatures around it. Males\nwill act as valets for those they serve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_morpeko" index="901">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it eats the seeds stored up in its\npouches, it generates electricity while\nsatisfying its constant hunger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cufant" index="902">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If a job requires serious strength,\nCufant will excel at it. Its copper body\ntarnishes in the rain, turning green.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_copperajah" index="903">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon live in herds. Their\ntrunks have incredible grip strength,\nstrong enough to crush giant rocks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dracozolt" index="904">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The powerful muscles in its tail\ngenerate its electricity. Its upper half\nis entirely too small. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_arctozolt" index="905">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The shaking of its freezing upper half\nis what generates its electricity. It has\na hard time walking around.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dracovish" index="906">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its mighty legs are capable of running\nat speeds exceeding 40 mph, but it can’t\nbreathe unless it’s underwater.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_arctovish" index="907">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The skin on its face is impervious\nto attack, but breathing difficulties\nmade it go extinct anyway.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_duraludon" index="908">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body resembles polished metal,\nand it’s both lightweight and strong.\nHowever, its body rusts easily.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dreepy" index="909">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">After being reborn as a ghost, Dreepy\nwanders the areas it used to inhabit back\nwhen it was alive in prehistoric seas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_drakloak" index="910">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s capable of flying faster than 120\nmph. It battles alongside Dreepy and\ndotes on them until they evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dragapult" index="911">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently the Dreepy inside its horns\neagerly look forward to being launched\nout at Mach speeds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zacian" index="912">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It  has slumbered for many years. Some\nsay it is Zamazenta’s elder sister,\nothers say the two are rivals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zamazenta" index="913">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It slept for aeons while in the form\nof a statue. It was asleep for so long,\npeople forgot that it ever existed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_eternatus" index="914">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was inside a meteorite that fell\n20,000 years ago. The energy that\nits core absorbs allows it to live.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kubfu" index="915">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it pulls the long white hair on\nits head, its fighting spirit heightens and\npower wells up from deep in its belly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_urshifu" index="916">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Inhabiting the mountains of a distant\nregion, it races across sheer cliffs,\ntraining its legs and refining its moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zarude" index="917">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once the vines on its body tear off,\nthey become nutrients in the soil. This\nhelps the plants of the forest grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_regieleki" index="918">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its entire body is made of an organ\nthat generates electricity.\nIt is capable of generating a\nregion’s worth of electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_regidrago" index="919">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of crystallized\ndragon energy. It is said to contain the\npower of every Dragon Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_glastrier" index="920">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Glastrier has tremendous physical\nstrength. The mask covering its face is\n100 times stronger than diamond.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_spectrier" index="921">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it dashes through the night,\nit absorbs the life energy of sleeping\nPokémon. It craves silence and solitude.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_calyrex" index="922">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its every move is filled with grace and\ndignity. Extremely intelligent, it is said\nto see past, present, and future events.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_basculegion" index="923">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is cloaked\nin the souls of its\ncomrades who perished during a punishing\njourney to the river of their birth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sneasler" index="924">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because of Sneasler’s virulent poison and\ndaunting physical prowess,\nno other species could hope to\nbest it on the frozen highlands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_overqwil" index="925">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Overqwil’s poisonous spikes\nwill reflexively react even\nwhile Overqwil sleeps, stabbing\nany moving thing that approaches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_enamorus" index="926">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it flies to this land from across\nthe sea, the bitter winter comes\nto an end. According to legend,\nthis Pokémon’s love gives rise to the\nbudding of fresh life across Hisui.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sprigatito" index="927">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The sweet scent its body gives off\nmesmerizes those around\nit. The scent grows\nstronger when this Pokémon is in the sun.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_floragato" index="928">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Floragato deftly wields the vine hidden\nbeneath its long fur, slamming the hard\nflower bud against its opponents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_meowscarada" index="929">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With skillful misdirection, it rigs\nfoes with pollen-packed flower\nbombs, and sets them off before\nits foes realize what’s going on.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fuecoco" index="930">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lies on warm rocks and uses the\nheat absorbed by its square-shaped\nscales to create fire energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_crocalor" index="931">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The combination of Crocalor’s fire energy\nand overflowing vitality has caused an\negg-shaped fireball\nto appear on its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_skeledirge" index="932">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Skeledirge’s gentle singing soothes\nthe souls of all that hear it. It burns\nits enemies to a crisp with flames\nof over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_quaxly" index="933">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its strong legs let it\neasily swim around in\neven fast-flowing rivers. It likes to keep\nthings tidy and is prone to overthinking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_quaxwell" index="934">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The hardworking Quaxwell\nobserves people and Pokémon from\nvarious regions and incorporates their\nmovements into its own dance routines.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_quaquaval" index="935">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Dancing in ways that evoke far-away\nplaces, this Pokémon mesmerizes all that\nsee it. Flourishes of its decorative\nwater feathers slice into its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lechonk" index="936">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon spurns all but the finest\nof foods. Its body gives off an herblike\nscent that bug Pokémon detest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_oinkologne" index="937">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Oinkologne is proud of its fine,\nglossy skin. It emits a concentrated\nscent from the tip of its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tarountula" index="938">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The ball of threads wrapped\naround its body is elastic enough\nto deflect the scythes of\nScyther, this Pokémon’s natural enemy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_spidops" index="939">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It clings to branches and ceilings\nusing its threads and moves without\na sound. It takes out its prey\nbefore the prey even notices it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_nymble" index="940">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has its third set of\nlegs folded up. When\nit’s in a tough spot, this Pokémon jumps\nover 30 feet using the\nstrength of its legs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lokix" index="941">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses its normally folded third set\nof legs when in Showdown Mode. This\nplaces a huge burden on its body, so\nit can’t stay in this mode for long.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pawmi" index="942">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The pads of its paws are\nelectricity-discharging organs. Pawmi\nfires electricity from its forepaws while\nstanding unsteadily on its hind legs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pawmo" index="943">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Pawmo uses a unique fighting technique\nin which it uses its forepaws to strike\nfoes and zap them with electricity\nfrom its paw pads simultaneously.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pawmot" index="944">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Pawmot’s fluffy fur acts as a battery.\nIt can store the same amount of\nelectricity as an electric car.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tandemaus" index="945">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The pair sticks together no matter what.\nThey split any food they find exactly\nin half and then eat it together.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_maushold" index="946">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The two little ones\njust appeared one day.\nThe group might be a family of related\nPokémon, but nobody knows for sure.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fidough" index="947">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The yeast in Fidough’s breath is useful\nfor cooking, so this Pokémon has been\nprotected by people since long ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dachsbun" index="948">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The surface of this Pokémon’s skin\nhardens when exposed to intense heat,\nand its body has an appetizing aroma.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_smoliv" index="949">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon converts nutrients\ninto oil, which it stores in the fruit\non its head. It can easily go a whole\nweek without eating or drinking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dolliv" index="950">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Dolliv shares its tasty,\nfresh-scented oil\nwith others. This species has coexisted\nwith humans since times long gone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_arboliva" index="951">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This calm Pokémon is very compassionate.\nIt will share its delicious, nutrient-rich\noil with weakened Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_squawkabilly" index="952">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon prefer to live in cities.\nThey form flocks based on the color of\ntheir feathers, and they\nfight over territory.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_nacli" index="953">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The ground scrapes its body\nas it travels, causing it to leave salt\nbehind. Salt is constantly being created\nand replenished inside Nacli’s body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_naclstack" index="954">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It compresses rock salt inside\nits body and shoots out hardened\nsalt pellets with enough force\nto perforate an iron sheet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_garganacl" index="955">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Garganacl will rub its fingertips together\nand sprinkle injured Pokémon\nwith salt. Even severe wounds\nwill promptly heal afterward.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_charcadet" index="956">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its firepower increases when it fights,\nreaching over 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit.\nIt likes berries that are rich in fat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_armarouge" index="957">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Armarouge evolved\nthrough the use of a set\nof armor that belonged to a distinguished\nwarrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ceruledge" index="958">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An old set of armor steeped in grudges\ncaused this Pokémon’s\nevolution. Ceruledge\ncuts its enemies to pieces without mercy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tadbulb" index="959">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate\nelectricity. If it senses danger,\nit will make its head blink\non and off to alert its allies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bellibolt" index="960">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">What appear to be eyeballs are actually\norgans for discharging the electricity\ngenerated by Bellibolt’s\nbelly-button dynamo.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wattrel" index="961">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon make their nests\non coastal cliffs. The nests\nhave a strange, crackling\ntexture, and they’re a popular delicacy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kilowattrel" index="962">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to\namplify its electricity. By riding the wind,\nthis Pokémon can fly\nover 430 miles in a day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_maschiff" index="963">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its well-developed jaw and fangs\nare strong enough to crunch\nthrough boulders, and its\nthick fat makes for an excellent defense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mabosstiff" index="964">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can store energy in its\nlarge dewlap. Mabosstiff unleashes this\nenergy all at once to blow away enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_shroodle" index="965">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To keep enemies away from its territory,\nit paints markings around its nest using\na poisonous liquid that has an acrid odor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_grafaiai" index="966">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Each Grafaiai paints its own individual\npattern, and it will\npaint that same pattern\nover and over again throughout its life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bramblin" index="967">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Not even Bramblin knows where\nit is headed as it tumbles\nacross the wilderness, blown\nby the wind. It loathes getting wet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_brambleghast" index="968">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Brambleghast wanders\naround arid regions.\nOn rare occasions, mass outbreaks of\nthese Pokémon will bury an entire town.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_toedscool" index="969">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Though it looks like Tentacool,\nToedscool is a completely different\nspecies. Its legs may be thin, but\nit can run at a speed of 30 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_toedscruel" index="970">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon gather into groups and\nform colonies deep within forests. They\nabsolutely hate it when\nstrangers approach.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_klawf" index="971">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon lives on sheer cliffs.\nIt sidesteps opponents’ attacks, then\nlunges for their weak\nspots with its claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_capsakid" index="972">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The more sunlight this Pokémon bathes in,\nthe more spicy chemicals are\nproduced by its body, and thus\nthe spicier its moves become.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_scovillain" index="973">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The red head converts spicy\nchemicals into fire energy and\nblasts the surrounding area\nwith a super spicy stream of flame.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rellor" index="974">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It rolls its mud ball\naround while the energy\nit needs for evolution matures.\nEventually the time\ncomes for it to evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rabsca" index="975">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The body that supports the\nball barely moves. Therefore, it is\nthought that the true body of this\nPokémon is actually inside the ball.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_flittle" index="976">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It spends its time running\naround wastelands. If anyone\nsteals its beloved berries, it will\nchase them down and exact its revenge.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_espathra" index="977">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It emits psychic power from the gaps\nbetween its multicolored frills and\nsprints at speeds greater than 120 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tinkatink" index="978">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swings its handmade hammer around to\nprotect itself, but the hammer is often\nstolen by Pokémon that eat metal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tinkatuff" index="979">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon make their homes in\npiles of scrap metal. They test the\nstrength of each other’s hammers\nby smashing them together.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tinkaton" index="980">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon has a very daring\ndisposition. It knocks\nrocks into the sky with\nits hammer, aiming for flying Corviknight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wiglett" index="981">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can pick up the scent\nof a Veluza just over 65 feet away\nand will hide itself in the sand.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wugtrio" index="982">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A variety of fish Pokémon,\nWugtrio was once considered\nto be a regional form of Dugtrio.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_bombirdier" index="983">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Bombirdier uses the apron\non its chest to bundle up food, which\nit carries back to its nest. It enjoys\ndropping things that make loud noises.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_finizen" index="984">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its water ring is made from seawater\nmixed with a sticky fluid that Finizen\nsecretes from its blowhole.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_palafin" index="985">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its physical capabilities are no different\nthan a Finizen’s, but\nwhen its allies are in danger, it\ntransforms and powers itself up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_varoom" index="986">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The steel section is Varoom’s actual\nbody. This Pokémon clings to rocks\nand converts the minerals within\ninto energy to fuel its activities.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_revavroom" index="987">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It creates a gas out\nof poison and minerals\nfrom rocks. It then detonates the gas\nin its eight cylinders\nto generate energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cyclizar" index="988">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can sprint at over 70 mph while\ncarrying a human. The rider’s\nbody heat warms Cyclizar’s\nback and lifts the Pokémon’s spirit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_orthworm" index="989">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When attacked, this Pokémon will wield the\ntendrils on its body like fists and pelt\nthe opponent with a storm of punches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_glimmet" index="990">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It absorbs nutrients from cave walls.\nThe petals it wears are made of\ncrystallized poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_glimmora" index="991">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When this Pokémon detects danger,\nit will open up its crystalline petals\nand fire beams from its conical body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_greavard" index="992">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that a dog Pokémon that died\nin the wild without ever interacting with\na human was reborn as this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_houndstone" index="993">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Houndstone spends most of its\ntime sleeping in graveyards.\nAmong all the dog Pokémon,\nthis one is most loyal to its master.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_flamigo" index="994">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon apparently ties\nthe base of its neck into a knot so\nthat the energy stored in its belly\ndoes not escape from its beak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cetoddle" index="995">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in frigid regions in pods of\nfive or so individuals. It loves the\nminerals found in snow and ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cetitan" index="996">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ice energy builds up in\nthe horn on its upper\njaw, causing the horn to reach cryogenic\ntemperatures that\nfreeze its surroundings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_veluza" index="997">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Veluza has excellent regenerative\ncapabilities. It sheds spare\nflesh from its body to boost its\nagility, then charges at its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dondozo" index="998">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is a glutton, but\nit’s bad at getting food. It teams\nup with a Tatsugiri to catch prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tatsugiri" index="999">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This is a small dragon Pokémon. It lives\ninside the mouth of Dondozo to protect\nitself from enemies on the outside.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_clodsire" index="1000">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives at the bottom of\nponds and swamps. It will carry\nWooper on its back and ferry\nthem across water from shore to shore.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kingambit" index="1001">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Only a Bisharp that stands above all\nothers in its vast army can evolve\ninto Kingambit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_great_tusk" index="1002">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This creature resembles a mysterious\nPokémon that, according to a paranormal\nmagazine, has lived since ancient times.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_scream_tail" index="1003">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a mysterious Pokémon\ndescribed in a paranormal magazine as a\nJigglypuff from one billion years ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_brute_bonnet" index="1004">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bears a slight resemblance\nto a Pokémon described in\na dubious magazine as a cross\nbetween a dinosaur and a mushroom.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_flutter_mane" index="1005">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has similar features\nto a ghostly pterosaur that was\ncovered in a paranormal magazine,\nbut the two have little else in common.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_slither_wing" index="1006">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon somewhat resembles an\nancient form of Volcarona that was\nintroduced in a dubious magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sandy_shocks" index="1007">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It slightly resembles a Magneton that\nlived for 10,000 years and was featured\nin an article in a paranormal magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_treads" index="1008">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon closely resembles\na scientific weapon that\na paranormal magazine claimed\nwas sent to this planet by aliens.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_bundle" index="1009">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its shape is similar to a robot\nfeatured in a paranormal magazine.\nThe robot was said to have been\ncreated by an ancient civilization.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_hands" index="1010">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is very similar to a\ncyborg covered by a paranormal\nmagazine. The cyborg was said to\nbe the modified form of a certain athlete.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_jugulis" index="1011">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s possible that Iron Jugulis,\nan object described in an old book,\nmay actually be this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_moth" index="1012">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon resembles an unknown object\ndescribed in a paranormal magazine\nas a UFO sent to observe humanity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_thorns" index="1013">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has some similarities to a Pokémon\nintroduced in a dubious magazine as a\nTyranitar from 1 billion\nyears in the future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_frigibax" index="1014">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon lives in forests and crags.\nUsing the power of its dorsal fin, it cools\nthe inside of its nest like a refrigerator.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_arctibax" index="1015">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Arctibax freezes the air around it,\nprotecting its face with an ice mask and\nturning its dorsal fin into a blade of ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_baxcalibur" index="1016">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon blasts cryogenic air\nout from its mouth. This air can\ninstantly freeze even liquid-hot lava.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gimmighoul" index="1017">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives inside an old treasure chest.\nSometimes it gets left\nin shop corners since\nno one realizes it’s actually a Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gholdengo" index="1018">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body seems to be\nmade up of 1,000 coins.\nThis Pokémon gets along well with others\nand is quick to make friends with anybody.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_wo_chien" index="1019">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It drains the life-force from vegetation,\ncausing nearby forests to instantly\nwither and fields to turn barren.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_chien_pao" index="1020">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can control 100\ntons of fallen snow. It plays\naround innocently by leaping\nin and out of avalanches it has caused.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ting_lu" index="1021">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The fear poured into an ancient ritual\nvessel has clad itself in rocks and\ndirt to become a Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_chi_yu" index="1022">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The envy accumulated within curved beads\nthat sparked multiple conflicts has clad\nitself in fire and become a Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_roaring_moon" index="1023">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">According to a dubious magazine,\nthis Pokémon has some connection to a\nphenomenon that occurs\nin a certain region.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_valiant" index="1024">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has some similarities to a\nmad scientist’s invention\ncovered in a paranormal magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_koraidon" index="1025">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon resembles Cyclizar, but it is\nfar burlier and more ferocious. Nothing is\nknown about its ecology\nor other features.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_miraidon" index="1026">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Much remains unknown about this\ncreature. It resembles Cyclizar, but\nit is far more ruthless and powerful.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_walking_wake" index="1027">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles an illustration published in\na paranormal magazine, said to be a\ndepiction of a super-ancient Suicune.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_leaves" index="1028">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Many of its physical\ncharacteristics match\nthose of a Virizion from the future that\nwas covered in a paranormal magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_poltchageist" index="1029">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Poltchageist looks like a regional form of\nSinistea, but it was recently discovered\nthat the two Pokémon\nare entirely unrelated.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sinistcha" index="1030">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It pretends to be tea,\ntrying to fool people\ninto drinking it so it can drain their life-\nforce. Its ruse is\ngenerally unsuccessful.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_okidogi" index="1031">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Okidogi is a ruffian with a short temper.\nIt can pulverize anything by swinging\naround the chain on its neck.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_munkidori" index="1032">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Munkidori keeps itself somewhere safe\nwhile it toys with its foes, using\npsychokinesis to induce\nintense dizziness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_fezandipiti" index="1033">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Fezandipiti beats its glossy wings to\nscatter pheromones that captivate\npeople and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ogerpon" index="1034">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This mischief-loving Pokémon is full of\ncuriosity. It battles by\ndrawing out the type-\nbased energy contained within its masks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_archaludon" index="1035">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It digs holes on mountains, searching\nfor food. It’s so durable that being\ncaught in a cave-in won’t faze it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gouging_fire" index="1036">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a Pokémon once shown in a\nparanormal magazine.\nThat Pokémon was said\nto be an Entei regenerated from a fossil.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_raging_bolt" index="1037">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bears resemblance to a Pokémon that\nbecame a hot topic for\na short while after\nbeing touted it as Raikou’s ancestor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_boulder" index="1038">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a Pokémon described in a\ndubious magazine as a Terrakion that had\nbeen modified by an evil organization.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_iron_crown" index="1039">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a mysterious object\nintroduced in a paranormal\nmagazine as a cutting-edge\nweapon shaped like a Cobalion.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_terapagos" index="1040">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s thought that this Pokémon lived\nin ancient Paldea until it got caught\nin seismic shifts and went extinct.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pecharunt" index="1041">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its peach-shaped shell\nserves as storage\nfor a potent poison. It makes poisonous\nmochi and serves it to\npeople and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_venusaur" index="1042">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By spreading the broad petals of\nits flower and catching the sun’s\nrays, it fills its body with power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_charizard_x" index="1043">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If CHARIZARD becomes furious,\nthe flame at the tip of its tail flares\nup in a light blue shade.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_charizard_y" index="1044">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If CHARIZARD becomes furious,\nthe flame at the tip of its tail flares\nup in a light blue shade.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_blastoise" index="1045">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It deliberately makes itself heavy\nso it can withstand the recoil\nof the water jets it fires.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_beedrill" index="1046">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can take down any opponent with\nits powerful poison stingers.\nIt sometimes attacks in swarms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_pidgeot" index="1047">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its well-developed chest muscles make\nit strong enough to whip up a gusty\nwindstorm with just a few flaps.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_alakazam" index="1048">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Closing both its eyes heightens all\nits other senses. This enables it to\nuse its abilities to their extremes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_slowbro" index="1049">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If the tail-biting SHELLDER is thrown\noff in a harsh battle, it reverts to\nbeing an ordinary SLOWPOKE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_gengar" index="1050">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It steals heat from its surroundings.\nIf you feel a sudden chill,\nit is certain that a GENGAR appeared.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_kangaskhan" index="1051">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it is safe, the young gets out of\nthe belly pouch to play. The adult\nkeeps a close eye on the youngster.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_pinsir" index="1052">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With its pincer horns, it digs burrows\nto sleep in at night. In the morning,\ndamp soil clings to its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_gyarados" index="1053">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They say that during past strife,\nGYARADOS would appear and leave\nblazing ruins in its wake.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_aerodactyl" index="1054">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A vicious Pokémon from the distant\npast, it appears to have flown by\nspreading its wings and gliding.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_mewtwo_x" index="1055">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because its battle abilities were\nraised to the ultimate level,\nit thinks only of defeating its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_mewtwo_y" index="1056">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because its battle abilities were\nraised to the ultimate level,\nit thinks only of defeating its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_ampharos" index="1057">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The tail’s tip shines brightly and\ncan be seen from far away. It acts\nas a beacon for lost people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_steelix" index="1058">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body has been compressed deep\nunder the ground. As a result,\nit is even harder than a diamond.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_scizor" index="1059">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swings its eye-patterned pincers\nup to scare its foes. This makes\nit look like it has three heads.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_heracross" index="1060">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This powerful Pokémon thrusts\nits prized horn under its enemies’\nbellies, then lifts and throws them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_houndoom" index="1061">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If you are burned by the flames\nit shoots from its mouth,\nthe pain will never go away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_tyranitar" index="1062">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body can’t be harmed by any\nsort of attack, so it is very eager\nto make challenges against enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_sceptile" index="1063">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It agilely leaps about the jungle\nand uses the sharp leaves on its\narms to strike its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_blaziken" index="1064">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can clear a 30-story building\nin a leap. Its fiery punches scorch\nits foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_swampert" index="1065">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its arms are hard as rock.\nWith one swing, it can\nbreak a boulder into pieces.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_gardevoir" index="1066">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It unleashes psychokinetic energy\nat full power when protecting a\nTrainer it has bonded closely with.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_sableye" index="1067">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It dwells in the darkness of caves.\nIt uses its sharp claws to dig up\ngems to nourish itself.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_mawile" index="1068">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It chomps with its gaping mouth.\nIts huge jaws are actually steel\nhorns that have been transformed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_aggron" index="1069">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">You can tell its age by the length\nof its iron horns. It claims an\nentire mountain as its territory.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_medicham" index="1070">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Through yoga training, it gained\nthe psychic power to predict\nits foe’s next move.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_manectric" index="1071">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its nest can be found where a\nthunderbolt hits. It is discharging\nelectricity from its mane.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_sharpedo" index="1072">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can swim at speeds of 75 mph by\njetting seawater through its body.\nIt is the bandit of the sea.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_camerupt" index="1073">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in the crater of a volcano.\nIt is well known that the humps on\nits back erupt every 10 years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_altaria" index="1074">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies gracefully through the\nsky. Its melodic humming makes\nyou feel like you’re in a dream.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_banette" index="1075">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon developed from an\nabandoned doll that amassed a\ngrudge. It is seen in dark alleys.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_absol" index="1076">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the ability to foretell\nnatural disasters. Its life span is\nover a hundred years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_glalie" index="1077">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can instantly freeze moisture in\nthe atmosphere. It uses this power\nto freeze its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_salamence" index="1078">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s uncontrollable if enraged.\nIt flies around spouting flames and\nscorching fields and mountains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_metagross" index="1079">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It folds its four legs when flying.\nIts four brains are said to be\nsuperior to a supercomputer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_latias" index="1080">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It communicates using telepathy.\nIts body is covered in down that\nrefracts light to make it invisible.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_latios" index="1081">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It understands human speech and is\nhighly intelligent. It is a tender\nPokémon that dislikes fighting.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_rayquaza" index="1082">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies in the ozone layer, way up\nhigh in the sky. Until recently,\nno one had ever seen it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_lopunny" index="1083">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sheds its fur twice a year.\nIts winter fur is soft and fluffy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_garchomp" index="1084">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is covered in fine scales that\nreduce drag, enabling it to fly at\nhigh speeds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_lucario" index="1085">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s said that no foe can remain invisible\nto LUCARIO, since it can detect auras.\nEven foes it could not otherwise see.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_abomasnow" index="1086">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives a quiet life on mountains that\nare perpetually covered in snow.\nIt hides itself by whipping up blizzards.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_gallade" index="1087">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it can sense what its foe\nis thinking, its attacks burst out\nfirst, fast, and fierce.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_audino" index="1088">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using the feelers on its ears,\nit can tell how someone is feeling\nor when an egg might hatch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mega_diancie" index="1089">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can instantly create many diamonds\nby compressing the carbon in the air\nbetween its hands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kyogre_primal" index="1090">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mythical Pokémon said to have\nswelled the seas with rain and tidal\nwaves. It battled with GROUDON.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_groudon_primal" index="1091">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Said to have expanded the lands by\nevaporating water with raging heat.\nIt battled titanically with KYOGRE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rattata_alolan" index="1092">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats anything. Wherever food is\navailable, it will settle down and\nproduce offspring continuously.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_raticate_alolan" index="1093">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Gnaws on anything with its tough\nfangs. It can even topple concrete\nbuildings by gnawing on them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_raichu_alolan" index="1094">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its electricity builds, its\nmuscles are stimulated, and it becomes\nmore aggressive than usual.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sandshrew_alolan" index="1095">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it fell from a great height, this\nPokémon could save itself by rolling\ninto a ball and bouncing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sandslash_alolan" index="1096">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In an attempt to hide itself,\nit will run around at top speed to\nkick up a blinding dust storm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vulpix_alolan" index="1097">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it develops, its single white\ntail gains color and splits into six.\nIt is quite warm and cuddly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ninetales_alolan" index="1098">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Some legends claim that each of its\nnine tails has its own unique type\nof special mystical power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_diglett_alolan" index="1099">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its skin is very thin. If it is exposed\nto light, its blood heats up,\ncausing it to grow weak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dugtrio_alolan" index="1100">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its three heads bob separately up\nand down to loosen the soil nearby,\nmaking it easier for it to burrow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_meowth_alolan" index="1101">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is fascinated by round objects.\nIt can’t stop playing with them\nuntil it tires and falls asleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_persian_alolan" index="1102">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Many adore it for its sophisticated air.\nHowever, it will lash out and\nscratch for little reason.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_geodude_alolan" index="1103">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Most people may not notice,\nbut a closer look should reveal that\nthere are many GEODUDE around.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_graveler_alolan" index="1104">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With a free and uncaring nature,\nit doesn’t mind if pieces break off\nwhile it rolls down mountains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_golem_alolan" index="1105">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sheds its skin once a year.\nThe discarded shell immediately\nhardens and crumbles away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_grimer_alolan" index="1106">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it moves, it loses bits of its body,\nfrom which new GRIMER emerge.\nThis worsens the stench around it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_muk_alolan" index="1107">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They love to gather in smelly areas\nwhere sludge accumulates, making\nthe stench around them worse.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_exeggutor_alolan" index="1108">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its three heads think independently.\nHowever, they are friendly and\nnever appear to squabble.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_marowak_alolan" index="1109">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has been seen pounding boulders\nwith the bone it carries in order\nto tap out messages to others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_raticate_alolan_large" index="1110">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Gnaws on anything with its tough\nfangs. It can even topple concrete\nbuildings by gnawing on them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_marowak_alolan_large" index="1111">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has been seen pounding boulders\nwith the bone it carries in order\nto tap out messages to others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gumshoos_large" index="1112">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Patient by nature, it loses control of\nitself and pounces when it spots its\nfavorite meal-Rattata!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_vikavolt_large" index="1113">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flusters opponents with acrobatic\nflying maneuvers. This creates an\nopening for it to attack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ribombee_large" index="1114">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Some of Ribombee’s pollen puffs are\nhighly nutritious. They are sometimes\nsold as supplements.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_araquanid_large" index="1115">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It delivers headbutts with the bubble\non its head. Small Pokémon get sucked\ninto it, where they drown.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_lurantis_large" index="1116">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For self-protection, it pretends to be\na bug Pokémon. Both of its arms bear\nkeen-edged petals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_salazzle_large" index="1117">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It punishes Salandit that couldn’t\nbring it food with a fierce slap of its\nflame-spewing palm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_togedemaru_large" index="1118">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it’s surprised or agitated, the 14\nfur spikes on its back will stand up\ninvoluntarily.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mimikyu_large" index="1119">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It conceals its terrifying appearance\nbeneath an old rag so it can get closer\nto people and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mimikyu_busted_large" index="1120">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It conceals its terrifying appearance\nbeneath an old rag so it can get closer\nto people and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kommo_o_large" index="1121">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It battles valiantly with its fists,\nwhich are armored in steel scales.\nKommo-o specializes in uppercuts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_meowth_galarian" index="1122">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is fascinated by round objects.\nIt can’t stop playing with them\nuntil it tires and falls asleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_ponyta_galarian" index="1123">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is a weak runner immediately\nafter birth. It gradually becomes\nfaster by chasing after its parents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_rapidash_galarian" index="1124">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">At full gallop, its four hooves\nbarely touch the ground because\nit moves so incredibly fast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_farfetchd_galarian" index="1125">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If anyone tries to disturb where the\nessential plant stalks grow, it uses its\nown stalk to thwart them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_weezing_galarian" index="1126">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If one of the twin KOFFING inflates,\nthe other one deflates. It constantly\nmixes its poisonous gases.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_mr_mime_galarian" index="1127">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A skilled mime from birth,\nit gains the ability to create\ninvisible objects as it matures.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_articuno_galarian" index="1128">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The magnificent, seemingly translucent\nwings of this legendary bird Pokémon\nare said to be made of ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zapdos_galarian" index="1129">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary bird Pokémon\ncauses savage thunderstorms by\nflapping its glittering wings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_moltres_galarian" index="1130">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary Pokémon scatters\nembers with every flap of its wings.\nIt is a thrilling sight to behold.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_slowking_galarian" index="1131">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has incredible intellect and\nintuition. Whatever the situation,\nit remains calm and collected.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_corsola_galarian" index="1132">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It continuously sheds and grows.\nThe tip of its head is prized as\na treasure because of its beauty.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_zigzagoon_galarian" index="1133">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gets interested in everything,\nwhich is why it zigs and zags.\nIt is good at finding items.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_linoone_galarian" index="1134">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When running in a straight line, it\ncan easily top 60 miles an hour. It\nhas a tough time with curved roads.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_darumaka_galarian" index="1135">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it sleeps, it pulls its limbs\ninto its body and its internal fire\ngoes down to 1,100 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_darmanitan_galarian" index="1136">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its internal fire burns at 2,500 degrees\nFahrenheit, making enough power that it\ncan destroy a dump truck with one punch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_yamask_galarian" index="1137">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon arose from the\nspirits of people interred in graves.\nEach retains memories of its former life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_stunfisk_galarian" index="1138">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its opponent can’t be paralyzed,\nit contorts itself with unexpected speed\nand flops away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_cosplay" index="1139">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_rock_star" index="1140">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_belle" index="1141">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_pop_star" index="1142">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_ph_d" index="1143">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_libre" index="1144">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_original_cap" index="1145">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_hoenn_cap" index="1146">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_sinnoh_cap" index="1147">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_unova_cap" index="1148">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_kalos_cap" index="1149">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_alola_cap" index="1150">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_partner_cap" index="1151">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_pikachu_world_cap" index="1152">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_castform_sunny" index="1153">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can change its cells,\ntaking different forms based on\nthe temperature and humidity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_castform_rainy" index="1154">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can change its cells,\ntaking different forms based on\nthe temperature and humidity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_castform_snowy" index="1155">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can change its cells,\ntaking different forms based on\nthe temperature and humidity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_cherrim_sunshine" index="1156">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">During times of strong sunlight,\nits bud blooms, its petals open\nfully, and it becomes very active.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_shellos_east_sea" index="1157">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its shape and coloration vary,\ndepending on its habitat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_gastrodon_east_sea" index="1158">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its natural enemy attacks,\nit oozes purple fluid and escapes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_dialga_origin" index="1159">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon completely controls the\nflow of time. It uses its power to travel\nat will through the past and future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_palkia_origin" index="1160">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its total control over the boundaries\nof space enable it to transport itself to\nfaraway places or even other dimensions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_basculin_blue_striped" index="1161">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Red- and blue-striped Basculin are\nvery violent and always fighting.\nThey are also remarkably tasty.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_basculin_white_striped" index="1162">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Red- and blue-striped Basculin are\nvery violent and always fighting.\nThey are also remarkably tasty.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_darmanitan_zen_mode" index="1163">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its internal fire burns at 2,500 degrees\nFahrenheit, making enough power that it\ncan destroy a dump truck with one punch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_darmanitan_zen_mode_galarian" index="1164">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its internal fire burns at 2,500 degrees\nFahrenheit, making enough power that it\ncan destroy a dump truck with one punch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_deerling_summer" index="1165">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their coloring changes according to the\nseasons and can be slightly affected\nby the temperature and humidity as well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_deerling_autumn" index="1166">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their coloring changes according to the\nseasons and can be slightly affected\nby the temperature and humidity as well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_deerling_winter" index="1167">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their coloring changes according to the\nseasons and can be slightly affected\nby the temperature and humidity as well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sawsbuck_summer" index="1168">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They migrate according to the seasons,\nso some people call Sawsbuck the\nharbingers of spring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sawsbuck_autumn" index="1169">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They migrate according to the seasons,\nso some people call Sawsbuck the\nharbingers of spring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_sawsbuck_winter" index="1170">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They migrate according to the seasons,\nso some people call Sawsbuck the\nharbingers of spring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_tornadus_therian" index="1171">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In every direction it flies,\ncreating winds so powerful,\nthey blow everything away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_thundurus_therian" index="1172">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it flies around, it shoots lightning all\nover the place and causes forest fires.\nIt is therefore disliked.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_landorus_therian" index="1173">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">From the forces of lightning and wind,\nit creates energy to give nutrients\nto the soil and make the land abundant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kyurem_white" index="1174">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary ice Pokémon waits for\na hero to fill in the missing parts\nof its body with truth or ideals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_kyurem_black" index="1175">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary ice Pokémon waits for\na hero to fill in the missing parts\nof its body with truth or ideals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_keldeo_resolute" index="1176">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it is resolute, its body fills\nwith power and it becomes swifter.\nIts jumps are then too fast to follow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_meloetta_pirouette" index="1177">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The melodies sung by Meloetta\nhave the power to make Pokémon\nthat hear them happy or sad.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_genesect_douse_drive" index="1178">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon existed 300 million\nyears ago. Team Plasma altered it\nand attached a cannon to its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_genesect_shock_drive" index="1179">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon existed 300 million\nyears ago. Team Plasma altered it\nand attached a cannon to its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_genesect_burn_drive" index="1180">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon existed 300 million\nyears ago. Team Plasma altered it\nand attached a cannon to its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0805_genesect_chill_drive" index="1181">
